WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:30.760
Everybody, so if you see a photo of us podcasting, I am now in my husband's closet.
各位，如果你们看到我们录播客的照片，我现在是在我丈夫的衣帽间里。

9
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:32.940
Those are not my baseball hats.
那些不是我的棒球帽。

10
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.600
That is his baseball hat collection.
那是他的棒球帽收藏。

11
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.340
I like to wear baseball hats.
我喜欢戴棒球帽。

12
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.120
You do.
你确实喜欢。

13
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.640
You are sort of like a baseball hat family.
你们家就像是个棒球帽家族。

14
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.560
I feel like all of your family loves baseball hats.
我觉得你们全家都爱戴棒球帽。

15
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:48.540
Oh, lady, one Christmas, we were trying to find a family photo that we could put on our Christmas card.
噢，亲爱的，有一年圣诞节，我们想找一张全家福印在圣诞贺卡上。

16
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.120
And I couldn't find one where one of us wasn't wearing a hat.
结果我一张都找不到，因为照片里总有人戴着帽子。

17
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.400
And so we decided to make it a bit.
于是我们决定把这变成一个梗。

18
00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.560
And we did a collage of just a baseball hat Christmas card.
我们做了一个全是棒球帽的拼贴画作为圣诞贺卡。

19
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.280
My mother-in-law was mortified.
我婆婆当时尴尬坏了。

20
00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:03.720
Mortified.
尴尬透了。

21
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.920
She's like, why are you all in hats?
她说，你们为什么都戴着帽子？

22
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.900
Yes, baseball hats for your formal Christmas card.
没错，戴着棒球帽拍正式的圣诞贺卡。

23
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.240
But yeah, it was like an inside joke.
但确实，这就像是个内部笑话。

24
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.200
We're a hat family.
我们就是个帽子家族。

25
00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.940
We would fit in very well in Josh's closet, I guess is what I'm saying.
我想说的是，我们应该会很适合待在乔什的衣帽间里。

26
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.700
I think you would.
我想你们会的。

27
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.240
By the way, side note, your Christmas cards are always awesome.
顺便提一下，你们的圣诞贺卡总是很棒。

28
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:28.640
My favorite, and I have it hanging up in the kitchen still, is the one where you guys are all holding Sunny, your cat.
我最喜欢的一张，现在还挂在我厨房里，就是你们全家抱着你们的猫桑尼的那张。

29
00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.980
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

30
00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.020
That was another fun collage.
那也是个有趣的拼贴画。

31
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.860
We had a good time with that.
我们当时玩得很开心。

32
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.640
Lee has Sunny on his head.
李把桑尼顶在头上。

33
00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.700
I'm holding Sunny upside down.
我把桑尼倒着抱。

34
00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.320
It was a good one.
那张真的很棒。

35
00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.140
Thanks, lady.
谢谢你，亲爱的。

36
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.100
You guys have a floppy cat.
你们养的是那种软绵绵的猫。

37
00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.120
And floppy cats are so great in photos.
这种猫拍照效果太好了。

38
00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.280
My cats would have, like, shredded our heads.
如果我试着那样做，我的猫大概会把我们的头抓烂。

39
00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.480
Look if we tried that.
如果我们试着那样做的话。

40
00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.200
Okay, okay.
好吧，好吧。

41
00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.500
So here we go.
那么我们开始吧。

42
00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.020
What are we doing today, Jenna?
我们今天要聊什么，珍娜？

43
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.520
Today we are talking about Season 3, Episode 12, Traveling Salesman.
今天我们要聊的是第三季第12集《旅行推销员》。

44
00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.080
Oh, it's so good.
噢，那一集太棒了。

45
00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.760
It's so good.
真的太棒了。

46
00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.340
I rewatched this one and The Return with my kids.
我和孩子们一起重温了这一集和《回归》那一集。

47
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.180
We all snuggled up in bed and watched them.
我们蜷在床上一起看了它们。

48
00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.440
They were laughing hysterically.
他们笑得前仰后合。

49
00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.600
Well, Angela, it's a good thing you watched those together.
安吉拉，你们一起看这两集真是太好了。

50
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:18.800
I did, too, because they were actually created to be kind of one big episode to be watched together.
我也这么做了，因为它们本来就是作为一整集大篇幅来创作的，适合连在一起看。

51
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:26.540
And that is why they were written by three writers, Mike Schur, Lee Eisenberg, and Gene Stupnitsky.
这就是为什么它们是由三位编剧迈克·舒尔、李·艾森伯格和吉恩·斯图普尼茨基共同创作的。

52
00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:30.320
And both of those episodes were directed by Greg Daniels.
这两集都是由格雷格·丹尼尔斯执导的。

53
00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.440
All right, Jenna, well, why don't you hit us with a summary?
好了，珍娜，你能不能给我们做个总结？

54
00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:33.180
All right.
好的。

55
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.900
So in Traveling Salesman, because that's the episode we're covering today,
在《旅行推销员》这一集中，因为这就是我们今天要讲的一集，

56
00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.640
Dwight covers for Angela after she misses an important deadline.
安吉拉错过了一个重要的截止日期，德怀特替她掩盖了过去。

57
00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.440
The sales team all pair up for sales calls.
销售团队的所有人都两两配对去进行销售拜访。

58
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:53.060
But at the same time, Angela uncharacteristically invites Pam to coffee and then discusses her love life.
但与此同时，安吉拉一反常态地邀请帕姆去喝咖啡，然后谈论起她的感情生活。

59
00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.880
In code, but she discusses her love life.
虽然是用暗语说的，但她确实谈论了她的感情生活。

60
00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:04.780
And then upon the return of the sales team, Michael learns that Dwight went to corporate behind his back.
然后当销售团队回来时，迈克尔得知德怀特背着他去找了公司高层。

61
00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.180
He doesn't know why.
他不知道原因。

62
00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.600
Dwight quits Dunder Mifflin.
德怀特从邓德·米夫林公司辞职了。

63
00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:10.980
Yes!
没错！

64
00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.240
And then Karen finds out that Jim once had a thing for Pam.
然后凯伦发现吉姆曾经对帕姆有意思。

65
00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.460
That's a lot of stuff.
这信息量真大。

66
00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.240
That's a lot of stuff.
这信息量真大。

67
00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.120
Phyllis, man.
菲利斯，天哪。

68
00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.240
She spilled the beans.
她把秘密泄露了。

69
00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:22.480
I know.
我知道。

70
00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:23.520
Phyllis.
菲利斯。

71
00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:24.660
Phyllis.
菲利斯。

72
00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:25.840
Okay, we'll get to that.
好吧，我们稍后会讲到那个。

73
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:26.680
We'll get to that.
我们稍后会讲到那个。

74
00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.440
I bet you have some really good fast facts.
我敢打赌你一定准备了一些很棒的速览小知识。

75
00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.000
Well, you know I do because you know that we got something.
嗯，你知道我准备了，因为你知道我们确实有些料。

76
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.400
We did.
我们确实有。

77
00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:35.320
All right.
好的。

78
00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.800
So here's what we got.
这就是我们准备的内容。

79
00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:38.560
All right.
好的。

80
00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:45.800
Fast fact number one, like I said, both this and the next episode, The Return, were written and treated like one big episode.
速览小知识第一条，正如我所说，这一集和下一集《回归》在创作和处理上都被视为一个大故事。

81
00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.500
They were both directed by Greg Daniels.
它们都是由格雷格·丹尼尔斯执导的。

82
00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.300
What did we do, Ange?
我们做了什么，安吉？

83
00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:51.680
Tell everybody what we did.
告诉大家我们做了什么。

84
00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:57.340
We reached out to Greg, and he sent in audio clips, and they are fantastic.
我们联系了格雷格，他发来了音频片段，真是太棒了。

85
00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.020
And now Jen and I want him to send in audio clips every single week.
现在我和珍都希望他每周都能发音频片段过来。

86
00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.080
Yes!
没错！

87
00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.420
His audio clips are so good, you guys.
伙计们，他的音频片段太棒了。

88
00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:05.520
We're giddy about them.
我们对此感到兴奋不已。

89
00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.200
And so the first thing we asked him was, what was the inspiration for this episode?
所以我们问他的第一个问题是，这一集的灵感来源是什么？

90
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.880
And here is what he had to say.
以下是他所说的。

91
00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:21.440
Traveling Salesman and The Return is a little two-episode arc that we did as part of the working out of the merger of the two branches stories.
《旅行推销员》和《回归》是我们为了处理两个分部合并的故事线而制作的一个两集小篇章。

92
00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:27.360
Andy was always conceived in Gay Witch Hunt to be the Stanford version of Dwight.
安迪在《同性恋猎巫》中被构思为斯坦福版的德怀特。

93
00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:31.160
So it was natural that they'd butt heads when the branches merged.
所以当两个分部合并时，他们发生冲突是很自然的。

94
00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:40.460
And we liked the idea that Dwight, as the hometown favorite, gets to have a really strong and romantic arc here.
我们喜欢这样一个想法，即作为本土宠儿的德怀特，在这里能有一个非常强烈且浪漫的故事线。

95
00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.040
You see a very noble side of him protecting the woman that he loves.
你看到了他保护自己所爱之人的非常高尚的一面。

96
00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:55.400
And I think one of the reasons we made it two episodes was it didn't feel real to me or earned to have him leave and come back in only one episode.
我认为我们把它拍成两集的原因之一是，如果只用一集就让他离开又回来，我觉得不够真实，也不够有说服力。

97
00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.120
So it just felt a lot better to spread it out over two.
所以把它分摊到两集里感觉好多了。

98
00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:06.680
And another part about that storyline was that it was pairings.
关于那个故事情节的另一个部分是角色配对。

99
00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:16.460
And, you know, a writing exercise that I often did with the writers was I'd have them try and come up with pairings of characters that we hadn't had scenes together before.
你知道，我经常和编剧们做的一个写作练习是，让他们尝试想出一些以前从未有过对手戏的角色组合。

100
00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:28.320
And so this entire episode was fun pairings like Ryan and Stanley or Phyllis and Karen and and of course, Angela and Pam,
所以整集都是有趣的配对，比如瑞安和斯坦利，或者菲利斯和凯伦，当然还有安吉拉和帕姆。

101
00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:35.420
who have a great emotional storyline where they really are kind of growing as as friends.
他们有着非常棒的情感故事线，在剧中作为朋友真正地成长了起来。

102
00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:40.600
And it was really cool to see Jim and Dwight, too, and see their backstory.
看到吉姆和德怀特也很酷，还能看到他们的背景故事。

103
00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:49.980
And then the other thing about Traveling Salesman was we used in the client, we used being good at sales to make Michael more likable.
关于《旅行推销员》这一集，另一件事是我们在客户身上运用了销售能力，让迈克尔变得更讨人喜欢了。

104
00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:56.300
And right, you know, in Traveling Salesman, you see a whole bunch of different characters and how they are as salespeople.
没错，你知道，在《旅行推销员》里，你可以看到一大堆不同的角色，以及他们作为销售人员的表现。

105
00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:07.400
And you see how how great Jim and Dwight work together and Michael being like a straight man for Andy, who's just terrible.
你可以看到吉姆和德怀特合作得有多棒，而迈克尔就像是安迪的捧哏，安迪简直太糟糕了。

106
00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:22.340
And so it kind of helps distinguish the more likable original Dwight versus the more sinister, schemey, you know, new Dwight.
这有助于区分那个更讨人喜欢的原始版德怀特，和那个更阴险、更爱耍心机的、你知道的，新版德怀特。

107
00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:23.740
Keep talking.
继续说。

108
00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:25.080
Talk forever, Greg.
一直说下去吧，格雷格。

109
00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:26.740
Greg, talk forever.
格雷格，一直说下去。

110
00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.440
It's so fascinating.
这太令人着迷了。

111
00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:34.040
I love that not only were there these new pairings of characters, but also of writers.
我喜欢这一点，不仅有这些新的角色组合，还有编剧们的新组合。

112
00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:36.180
It's just so interesting.
这真的太有趣了。

113
00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.200
Yes.
是的。

114
00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:39.040
Yes, Ange.
没错，安吉。

115
00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:46.080
And so much comes out in this episode when you put these different people together for the first time, really.
当把这些不同的人第一次真正聚在一起时，这一集里展现出了很多东西。

116
00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:47.500
Yeah.
是啊。

117
00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:58.840
So you guys, I don't know if we need to start some sort of a petition, but we really want to create a new feature of the show called Inspiration with Greg.
所以伙计们，我不知道我们是否需要发起某种请愿，但我们真的很想在节目中创建一个名为“格雷格的灵感”的新板块。

118
00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:04.280
And he will send us an audio clip of the inspiration behind every episode.
他会给我们发送一段音频剪辑，讲述每一集背后的灵感来源。

119
00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:05.660
And there's like piano music.
还会配上钢琴音乐。

120
00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.440
Greg will tell us the inspiration.
格雷格会告诉我们灵感来源。

121
00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:12.040
And then Kent tells us the nuts and bolts of how he made that inspiration happen.
然后肯特会告诉我们他是如何具体实现这些灵感的细节。

122
00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.100
Greg is listening right now.
格雷格现在正在听呢。

123
00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.040
And I was like, ladies, what are you signing me up for?
当时我就想，女士们，你们这是给我报了什么名啊？

124
00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:16.920
Exactly.
正是如此。

125
00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.240
What is Fast Fact No.
第二个冷知识是什么？

126
00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:19.640
2?
2？

127
00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:24.900
Well, Angela, speaking of Kentopedia, Fast Fact No.
嗯，安吉拉，说到“肯特百科”，第二个冷知识叫做“地点，地点，还是地点”。

128
00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.060
2 is called Locations, Locations, Locations.
2叫做“地点，地点，还是地点”。

129
00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:37.440
So for this episode, because we actually shot it in conjunction with the return, we did something called crossboarding.
所以对于这一集，因为我们实际上是和《回归》那一集一起拍摄的，我们做了一些叫做“交叉拍摄”的事情。

130
00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:41.520
It's a little lingo that they use in the biz.
这是他们在业内使用的一点行话。

131
00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:50.360
So crossboarding is when you shoot two episodes at once.
所以交叉拍摄就是同时拍摄两集内容。

132
00:07:50.500 --> 00:08:01.620
We normally shot one episode each week, but we shot these episodes over a 10-day period from October 16, 2006 to October 27, 2006.
我们通常每周拍一集，但这两集我们是在2006年10月16日到2006年10月27日这10天内拍完的。

133
00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:06.280
And the main reason for this was because of locations.
而这背后的主要原因就是地点问题。

134
00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:11.140
Locations, we just had a lot of places to go in these two episodes.
地点，我们在这两集里要去的地方实在太多了。

135
00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:15.320
And having the flexibility to shoot it over a two-week period was really helpful.
能够灵活地在两周内完成拍摄真的很有帮助。

136
00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:16.160
Yes.
是的。

137
00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.900
And they would also do a thing, you guys.
而且他们还会做一件事，伙计们。

138
00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.940
They call it shooting out a location.
