450
00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:25.850
You guys are kind of talking in code.
你们俩在用暗语交流。

451
00:23:25.850 --> 00:23:28.230
But, of course, Pam is clocking it all.
但当然，帕姆把这一切都看在眼里。

452
00:23:28.430 --> 00:23:32.550
And then as you walk away, you say, I don't want these.
然后当你走开时，你说，我不想要这些。

453
00:23:32.730 --> 00:23:34.350
And you leave the jelly beans.
然后你就把软糖留下了。

454
00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:36.730
We had a fan question.
我们有一个粉丝提问。

455
00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:46.230
Allie Jo Higginbotham says, did Angela improv that line, I don't want these, to Pam after she took the jelly beans?
艾莉·乔·希金博瑟姆问，安吉拉在拿走软糖后对帕姆说的那句“我不想要这些”，是即兴发挥的吗？

456
00:23:47.290 --> 00:23:47.850
Yes.
是的。

457
00:23:48.330 --> 00:23:49.430
Yes, I did.
是的，是我即兴说的。

458
00:23:50.190 --> 00:23:57.110
The note that Greg had given me in that scene is that, you know, I'm so anxious to talk to Dwight to find out that everything went okay.
格雷格在那场戏里给我的指示是，你知道，我非常急切地想和德怀特谈谈，确认一切是否顺利。

459
00:23:57.110 --> 00:23:59.670
But I had to make some business for myself.
但我得给自己找点事做。

460
00:23:59.810 --> 00:24:01.050
Like, why would I be at reception?
比如，我为什么会在前台呢？

461
00:24:01.470 --> 00:24:03.990
So, I decided to kind of dig in the jelly beans.
所以，我决定去翻翻那些软糖。

462
00:24:04.130 --> 00:24:06.210
I just sort of was like, oh, this is what I'll do.
我当时就想，哦，我就这么做吧。

463
00:24:06.610 --> 00:24:08.250
So, I was digging in the jelly beans.
于是，我就在翻那些软糖。

464
00:24:08.390 --> 00:24:10.450
And I put a few in my hand throughout the scene.
在整场戏里，我往手里抓了几颗。

465
00:24:10.450 --> 00:24:13.450
And then as Dwight walked away, I just had him in my hand.
然后当德怀特走开时，我手里还抓着它们。

466
00:24:13.570 --> 00:24:16.150
So, I just placed him on the countertop.
所以，我就把它们放在了柜台上。

467
00:24:16.270 --> 00:24:17.050
Like your kid would.
就像你孩子会做的那样。

468
00:24:17.190 --> 00:24:18.030
I don't want this.
我不想要这个。

469
00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:18.770
Yes.
没错。

470
00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:19.730
He just walked away.
他直接走开了。

471
00:24:20.090 --> 00:24:22.510
And it just tickled us so much.
这让我们觉得特别好笑。

472
00:24:22.510 --> 00:24:23.650
And they left it in.
而且他们把这一幕留在了正片里。

473
00:24:23.790 --> 00:24:28.170
But the part I love even more, Jenna, is your look.
但珍娜，我更喜欢的部分是你的表情。

474
00:24:28.330 --> 00:24:32.930
Your look of like, it said so much to me in the moment.
你那种表情，在那一刻对我来说传达了太多信息。

475
00:24:33.090 --> 00:24:38.510
It said people leave their water bottles and their trash on my desk.
那表情仿佛在说，人们总是把水瓶和垃圾留在我的桌子上。

476
00:24:38.830 --> 00:24:38.910
Constantly.
没完没了。

477
00:24:38.930 --> 00:24:39.690
All the time.
一直都是这样。

478
00:24:39.690 --> 00:24:44.070
After you would leave the jelly beans, I added a little bit that got cut out.
在你留下软糖之后，我还加了一小段戏，不过被剪掉了。

479
00:24:44.230 --> 00:24:47.130
And probably it should have been cut out because it just would have gone on forever.
可能确实应该剪掉，因为如果不剪的话，那段戏就没完没了了。

480
00:24:47.430 --> 00:24:51.750
But I would find all these various ways to get rid of the jelly beans.
但我当时想出了各种方法来处理掉那些软糖。

481
00:24:51.950 --> 00:24:57.250
So, I remember one time I picked up the trash can and I scooched them into the trash can using a piece of paper.
我记得有一次我拿起垃圾桶，用一张纸把它们扫进了垃圾桶里。

482
00:24:57.470 --> 00:25:02.330
And another time I like took a tissue and I picked them up with a tissue.
还有一次，我拿了一张纸巾，用纸巾把它们捡起来。

483
00:25:03.330 --> 00:25:07.550
And another time I think I picked them up and put them back in the jelly bean container.
还有一次，我想我是把它们捡起来，又放回了软糖罐子里。

484
00:25:07.850 --> 00:25:08.010
Ew!
咦！

485
00:25:08.010 --> 00:25:12.910
I had, I know, I had all these ways that I got rid of these jelly beans.
我知道，我当时想出了各种办法来处理这些软糖。

486
00:25:13.190 --> 00:25:14.950
And I had a good time with that.
我玩得很开心。

487
00:25:15.150 --> 00:25:16.470
None of them made it in, of course.
当然，这些都没能出现在正片里。

488
00:25:16.690 --> 00:25:20.030
But it was just kind of like a fun little bit we were doing.
但这只是我们当时玩的一个有趣的小花絮。

489
00:25:20.310 --> 00:25:23.070
So, should we move into the conference room now, Angela?
那么，安吉拉，我们现在要转场到会议室了吗？

490
00:25:23.770 --> 00:25:24.530
Oh, yeah.
哦，好的。

491
00:25:24.650 --> 00:25:27.650
Because somebody needs to pass the tardy sauce.
因为有人得递一下“迟到酱”。

492
00:25:27.650 --> 00:25:33.090
Yes, the entire sales team is assembled in the conference room and Dwight comes in late.
是的，整个销售团队都在会议室集合了，德怀特迟到了。

493
00:25:33.450 --> 00:25:35.390
So, Andy is such a tool.
安迪真是个十足的蠢货。

494
00:25:35.650 --> 00:25:36.570
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

495
00:25:36.830 --> 00:25:42.270
So, at the beginning of this scene, Michael explains that this is his dream team.
在这场戏的开头，迈克尔解释说这是他的梦之队。

496
00:25:42.270 --> 00:25:44.270
This is my dream sales team.
这是我的梦幻销售团队。

497
00:25:44.270 --> 00:25:46.930
And we're going to pair up and go on some sales calls.
我们要两两分组去进行销售拜访。

498
00:25:46.930 --> 00:25:50.810
And we had a fan question from Holly Ennarson.
我们收到了来自霍莉·恩纳森的粉丝提问。

499
00:25:51.430 --> 00:25:53.290
Holly Ennarson says,
霍莉·恩纳森问，

500
00:25:53.510 --> 00:25:57.670
Phyllis blows her nose right after Michael says,
菲利斯在迈克尔说完话后立刻擤了鼻子，

501
00:25:57.890 --> 00:25:59.650
This is my dream team.
这是我的梦之队。

502
00:25:59.790 --> 00:26:01.650
Was that scripted?
那是写好的剧本吗？

503
00:26:01.790 --> 00:26:04.550
I wondered the same thing because it's brilliant.
我也在想这个问题，因为太精彩了。

504
00:26:04.550 --> 00:26:06.430
The timing is so perfect.
时机把握得太完美了。

505
00:26:06.830 --> 00:26:08.110
It's so perfect.
简直太完美了。

506
00:26:09.090 --> 00:26:10.690
Yes, it was scripted.
是的，那是写好的剧本。

507
00:26:11.030 --> 00:26:11.310
Amazing.
太棒了。

508
00:26:11.970 --> 00:26:13.630
Here is the script direction.
这是剧本说明。

509
00:26:14.270 --> 00:26:14.830
Quote,
引用如下：

510
00:26:15.430 --> 00:26:18.490
The camera pans to bored faces of the sales team.
镜头扫过销售团队无聊的脸。

511
00:26:18.890 --> 00:26:20.450
Phyllis blows her nose.
菲利斯擤了擤鼻子。

512
00:26:22.750 --> 00:26:27.690
And, you know, guys, this is a little moment because I watched it several times.
伙计们，你们知道吗，这是一个很小的细节，因为我看了好几遍。

513
00:26:28.670 --> 00:26:29.850
It's so great.
真是太棒了。

514
00:26:30.350 --> 00:26:32.030
Phyllis gets out her little tissue.
菲利斯拿出了她的小纸巾。

515
00:26:32.290 --> 00:26:34.070
She sniffles a little bit.
她吸了吸鼻子。

516
00:26:34.250 --> 00:26:35.790
And then she blows her nose.
然后她擤了擤鼻子。

517
00:26:35.790 --> 00:26:40.810
Like, she times it perfectly, but she starts the bit a little early.
她时机把握得很好，但她开始得有点早。

518
00:26:41.450 --> 00:26:44.630
And I think that's what sells making it look so organic.
我觉得正是这一点让它看起来如此自然。

519
00:26:44.870 --> 00:26:46.990
It's really wonderful work.
这真是非常精彩的表演。

520
00:26:47.130 --> 00:26:48.150
Little details.
小细节。

521
00:26:48.470 --> 00:26:50.710
Phyllis, man, with the tissue work.
菲利斯，天哪，那纸巾用得真绝。

522
00:26:50.870 --> 00:26:52.670
So everyone gets paired up.
所以每个人都被分成了小组。

523
00:26:52.910 --> 00:27:01.110
Yes, we get Karen and Phyllis and Ryan and Stanley, Dwight and Jim, and Michael and Andy.
没错，凯伦和菲利斯一组，瑞安和斯坦利一组，德怀特和吉姆一组，迈克尔和安迪一组。

524
00:27:01.310 --> 00:27:04.870
Now they're going to go out and be in cars together all day.
现在他们要一起开车出去待上一整天。

525
00:27:04.870 --> 00:27:05.870
I couldn't wait.
我简直等不及了。

526
00:27:06.030 --> 00:27:08.370
I remember when we got the script, Jenna, at the table read.
珍娜，我记得我们拿到剧本的时候，是在剧本围读会上。

527
00:27:08.530 --> 00:27:12.490
When I saw, like, the groupings, I was like, oh, this is going to be so fun.
当我看到分组的时候，我就想，噢，这一定会很有趣。

528
00:27:12.850 --> 00:27:17.330
Well, there's a Ryan talking head in here that makes me laugh so hard.
对了，这里有个瑞安的采访镜头让我笑得不行。

529
00:27:17.610 --> 00:27:19.730
Because you are now Ryan in real life.
因为你在现实生活中现在就是瑞安。

530
00:27:19.770 --> 00:27:20.710
I am now Ryan.
我现在就是瑞安。

531
00:27:21.370 --> 00:27:26.490
I love it that he said he's flattered to be Stanley's second choice after pass.
他说他很荣幸能成为斯坦利在拒绝之后第二选择，我太喜欢这段了。

532
00:27:28.210 --> 00:27:29.070
After pass.
在拒绝之后。

533
00:27:29.070 --> 00:27:31.170
But Stanley got to pick his partner.
但斯坦利是可以选搭档的。

534
00:27:31.390 --> 00:27:33.390
And his first response was pass.
他的第一反应是拒绝。

535
00:27:33.790 --> 00:27:36.930
And his second response was, I guess he'll take the kid.
而他的第二反应是，我想他只能带上这孩子了。

536
00:27:37.690 --> 00:27:41.070
Well, I wanted to talk really quickly about Jim's talking head.
对了，我想快速聊聊吉姆的采访镜头。

537
00:27:41.290 --> 00:27:45.170
He holds up that photo of Dwight and Jim, like the old photo.
他举起了一张德怀特和吉姆的照片，就是那张旧照片。

538
00:27:45.350 --> 00:27:49.990
Because they clearly have been on a ton of sales calls together, right?
因为他们显然一起跑过很多次销售，对吧？

539
00:27:49.990 --> 00:27:53.270
And it shows their history a little bit, which I love.
这稍微展示了一下他们的过往，我非常喜欢。

540
00:27:53.430 --> 00:28:00.210
But in the DVD commentary, Rain said that his hair in that photo was from 1991.
但在DVD评论音轨里，雷恩说照片里他的头发是1991年的。

541
00:28:00.530 --> 00:28:04.410
He was on tour with an acting company doing Romeo and Juliet.
当时他正随一个剧团巡演，演的是《罗密欧与朱丽叶》。

542
00:28:04.590 --> 00:28:07.170
And they all had long Elizabethan hair.
他们当时都留着伊丽莎白时代的长发。

543
00:28:10.370 --> 00:28:14.710
And they sort of, they sort of, like, Photoshopped it onto current Dwight.
他们大概是把那头发PS到了现在的德怀特身上。

544
00:28:14.810 --> 00:28:16.010
But they left that big hair.
但他们保留了那头长发。

545
00:28:16.150 --> 00:28:17.090
I just thought it was hilarious.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

546
00:28:17.610 --> 00:28:19.470
I love that detail.
我喜欢这个细节。

547
00:28:19.770 --> 00:28:20.490
I know.
我也是。

548
00:28:21.090 --> 00:28:23.030
So now they're all in the parking lot.
现在他们都在停车场了。

549
00:28:23.190 --> 00:28:24.310
They're paired up into their teaMs.
他们已经分好了组。

550
00:28:24.490 --> 00:28:26.030
They're about to get in their cars and go.
他们正准备上车出发。

551
00:28:26.650 --> 00:28:31.250
Michael tosses Dwight his dirty laundry, which is a callback to the coup.
迈克尔把脏衣服扔给德怀特，这是对政变情节的呼应。

552
00:28:31.790 --> 00:28:34.090
I love it when our show does this.
我喜欢我们剧集里这种设计。

553
00:28:34.190 --> 00:28:35.630
And we have a few in this episode.
这一集里还有好几处这样的呼应。

554
00:28:35.810 --> 00:28:37.410
But this is a callback to the coup.
但这一处是对政变情节的呼应。

555
00:28:37.830 --> 00:28:39.990
And now he tells them all to circle up.
现在他让大家围过来。

556
00:28:40.070 --> 00:28:42.010
And he's going to give them their marching orders.
他要给他们下达指令了。

557
00:28:42.890 --> 00:28:43.150
Yeah.
没错。

558
00:28:43.150 --> 00:28:47.870
So then Michael says, guys, let's go out on our sales calls.
然后迈克尔说，伙计们，我们去跑销售吧。

559
00:28:48.010 --> 00:28:50.170
This is, it's like the, we're the amazing race.
这就像是，我们是在参加《极速前进》一样。

560
00:28:50.330 --> 00:28:53.030
And everyone's like, how are we the amazing race?
大家都一脸困惑，我们怎么就成《极速前进》了？

561
00:28:53.030 --> 00:28:53.970
Is there a prize?
有奖金吗？

562
00:28:54.150 --> 00:28:55.390
He's like, no, there's no prize.
他说，没有，没奖金。

563
00:28:55.390 --> 00:28:57.190
But we're the amazing race.
但我们就是《极速前进》。

564
00:28:57.190 --> 00:28:59.730
And he keeps, gives everybody these team names.
他不停地给每个人起队名。

565
00:29:00.190 --> 00:29:01.910
And everyone's very confused.
大家都感到非常困惑。

566
00:29:01.930 --> 00:29:03.770
And then Michael just gets frustrated.
然后迈克尔就变得很沮丧。

567
00:29:04.090 --> 00:29:05.950
He's like, just go on your sales call.
他说，你们就去跑销售吧。

568
00:29:06.290 --> 00:29:09.350
But I love that he brought up the amazing race.
但我很喜欢他提到《极速前进》这一点。

569
00:29:09.350 --> 00:29:12.470
This was a really, really popular reality show at the time.
那是当时非常、非常火的一档真人秀节目。

570
00:29:12.610 --> 00:29:14.130
And I was a huge fan.
我当时是它的超级粉丝。

571
00:29:14.750 --> 00:29:16.610
Jenna, we were so into it.
珍娜，我们当时特别迷那个节目。

572
00:29:16.730 --> 00:29:18.750
I remember you and I watching the amazing race.
我记得你和我一起看《极速前进》来着。

573
00:29:18.910 --> 00:29:21.990
And then Jenna, do you remember how you and I were like, we should go on.
珍娜，你还记得你我当时说我们应该去参加吗？

574
00:29:22.110 --> 00:29:24.390
We should be a team on amazing race together.
我们应该一起组队去参加《极速前进》。

575
00:29:24.970 --> 00:29:26.070
I stand by that.
我依然坚持这个想法。

576
00:29:26.250 --> 00:29:26.930
I think we should.
我觉得我们应该去。

577
00:29:27.130 --> 00:29:29.250
I think we, we would have been amazing.
我觉得我们肯定会表现得很棒。

578
00:29:29.770 --> 00:29:32.010
I think we would have been a total mess.
我觉得我们肯定会乱成一团。

579
00:29:32.770 --> 00:29:33.170
Why?
为什么？

580
00:29:34.070 --> 00:29:34.470
Why?
为什么？

581
00:29:35.470 --> 00:29:38.590
Because I think you would be like, let's go, let's go.
因为我觉得你会一直催，快走，快走。

582
00:29:38.590 --> 00:29:40.090
And I'd be like, can we just take a break?
而我会说，我们能休息一下吗？

583
00:29:40.250 --> 00:29:41.330
Maybe we'll have a glass of wine.
也许我们该喝杯红酒。

584
00:29:41.490 --> 00:29:42.170
You'd be like, yeah, yeah.
你肯定会说，好吧，好吧。

585
00:29:43.670 --> 00:29:46.230
Also, I can't eat any of that gross stuff, lady.
而且，我可吃不了那些恶心的东西，大姐。

586
00:29:46.350 --> 00:29:47.490
I can't eat the gross stuff.
我吃不了那些恶心的东西。

587
00:29:47.890 --> 00:29:49.110
Well, this is the problem.
嗯，这就是问题所在。

588
00:29:49.310 --> 00:29:52.490
I think we would both have some of the same weaknesses.
我觉得我们俩会有一些共同的弱点。

589
00:29:52.910 --> 00:29:54.810
I think we couldn't eat the gross stuff.
我觉得我们都吃不了那些恶心的东西。

590
00:29:54.990 --> 00:29:59.450
And maybe neither one of us would have great upper body strength for some of the, like,
而且可能我们俩的上肢力量都不怎么样，应付不了那些，比如，

591
00:30:00.190 --> 00:30:04.710
things where you have to, like, like, toss bales of hay down a maze or something.
那些需要你，比如，把草垛扔过迷宫之类的任务。

592
00:30:04.970 --> 00:30:07.250
How about zero upper body strength?
上肢力量为零怎么样？

593
00:30:07.450 --> 00:30:07.790
Yeah.
没错。

594
00:30:07.790 --> 00:30:08.730
Like, zero.
就是，完全为零。

595
00:30:09.110 --> 00:30:12.330
So maybe we wouldn't have been such a great team, but we would have had fun.
所以也许我们组队表现不会太好，但我们会玩得很开心。

596
00:30:12.830 --> 00:30:14.110
I think we would have had fun.
我觉得我们会玩得很开心。

597
00:30:14.250 --> 00:30:17.570
I think we would have had one colossal meltdown and then a fight.
我觉得我们会彻底崩溃，然后大吵一架。

598
00:30:17.590 --> 00:30:18.910
And then we would have cried.
然后我们会哭。

599
00:30:18.950 --> 00:30:20.830
And then we'd laugh hysterically.
接着又会歇斯底里地大笑。

600
00:30:21.030 --> 00:30:23.390
We'd look like crazy people.
看起来就像疯子一样。

601
00:30:23.530 --> 00:30:24.730
But we would have had fun.
但我们本来会玩得很开心的。

602
00:30:24.890 --> 00:30:26.990
I tell you what, we would have been good TV.
跟你说吧，我们本来会成为很好的电视节目的。

603
00:30:27.590 --> 00:30:28.490
Oh, my God.
天哪。

604
00:30:28.490 --> 00:30:29.910
We would have been great TV.
我们本来会成为很棒的电视节目的。

605
00:30:31.930 --> 00:30:32.630
Okay, okay.
好了，好了。

606
00:30:32.630 --> 00:30:35.910
Well, we actually asked Greg about this Amazing Race moment.
其实我们问过格雷格关于这个《极速前进》桥段的事。

607
00:30:35.910 --> 00:30:37.290
And here's what he had to say.
这是他给出的回应。

608
00:30:37.770 --> 00:30:40.990
The comparison to Amazing Race was fun.
拿《极速前进》做类比很有趣。

609
00:30:41.150 --> 00:30:44.810
Because it's a reality, we were a reality-based comedy show.
因为这是一种真人秀，而我们是一部基于真人秀形式的喜剧。

610
00:30:44.810 --> 00:30:55.190
It was a lot easier for the visual look of the show to be able to try and do references to other reality shows rather than movies, for instance.
相比于电影，在视觉上参考其他真人秀节目要容易得多。

611
00:30:55.190 --> 00:30:59.810
So there's like a Titanic reference in Booz Cruise.
所以像《酒后巡游》里就有个致敬《泰坦尼克号》的桥段。

612
00:30:59.810 --> 00:31:07.390
But I don't think it works as visually well as Amazing Race reference for here.
但我觉得视觉效果上不如这里的《极速前进》梗好用。

613
00:31:08.510 --> 00:31:08.690
Yeah.
没错。

614
00:31:09.030 --> 00:31:10.990
It totally makes sense to me, though.
不过我完全理解。

615
00:31:11.190 --> 00:31:15.250
I think Michael is such a fan of pop culture and television and film.
我觉得迈克尔是个流行文化、电视和电影的超级粉丝。

616
00:31:15.390 --> 00:31:23.150
Like, he wants any opportunity for his documentary of this paper company, whatever this is, this camera crew that follows him around.
他想抓住任何机会，让他的这家造纸公司纪录片——不管这到底是什么——让这些跟拍他的摄像团队拍出点名堂。

617
00:31:23.210 --> 00:31:26.910
He thinks he's on par with the entertainment of the day.
他觉得自己和当下的娱乐节目水平相当。

618
00:31:27.330 --> 00:31:27.690
Yes.
是的。

619
00:31:28.110 --> 00:31:28.530
Yes.
没错。

620
00:31:28.530 --> 00:31:34.130
Well, so now everyone gets in their cars and we kind of start driving around.
好了，现在大家都上了车，我们开始四处兜风了。

621
00:31:34.430 --> 00:31:41.010
And Angela, speaking of driving, we had a lot of questions about how we pulled off these driving shots.
安吉拉，说到开车，我们收到了很多关于这些驾驶镜头是怎么拍出来的问题。

622
00:31:41.950 --> 00:31:50.530
Amy Jackson, DeAndra Tassone, Holly E., TJ McMillan, William Burke, and many more people all asked,
艾米·杰克逊、迪安德拉·塔索内、霍莉·E、TJ·麦克米伦、威廉·伯克，还有更多人都问了：

623
00:31:50.690 --> 00:31:53.770
How did filming work for the driving scenes?
驾驶场景是怎么拍摄的？

624
00:31:53.830 --> 00:31:57.230
Are you guys actually driving or is there a green screen?
你们是真的在开车，还是用了绿幕？

625
00:31:57.850 --> 00:31:59.970
What cameras were used in the car scenes?
车内场景用了什么摄像机？

626
00:32:00.170 --> 00:32:02.790
And are the actors really driving around?
演员们是真的在开车吗？

627
00:32:03.510 --> 00:32:06.150
Well, first of all, the actors really are driving around.
首先，演员们确实是在开车。

628
00:32:06.290 --> 00:32:07.310
That is not a green screen.
那不是绿幕。

629
00:32:07.730 --> 00:32:13.670
And then we went to Greg and we asked him to talk a little bit about what it was like to shoot people in the cars.
然后我们去找格雷格，请他谈谈拍摄车内戏份是什么感觉。

630
00:32:13.670 --> 00:32:15.030
And here's what he had to say.
这是他的回应。

631
00:32:15.230 --> 00:32:23.210
And one of the things I had noticed in production was how easy it was to shoot in a car for our show.
我在制作过程中注意到的一点是，在我们的节目里，车内拍摄是多么容易。

632
00:32:23.370 --> 00:32:29.730
You just basically put the two characters in the car and set up lipstick cameras and drove around and improvised a lot.
你基本上只要把两个角色放进车里，架上微型摄像机，开车到处转，然后进行大量的即兴表演就行了。

633
00:32:29.730 --> 00:32:39.650
And so the idea for a traveling salesman was we could get a lot of production value out of getting out of the office and it wouldn't be too hard for us to do.
所以关于推销员出差的构思是，我们可以通过走出办公室获得很高的制作价值，而且这对我们来说并不难。

634
00:32:39.790 --> 00:32:43.830
We just tricked out these cars and they would go off.
我们只要把这些车改装好，他们就能出发了。

635
00:32:43.830 --> 00:32:48.750
So we have a little lingo alert there when Greg talks about lipstick cameras.
这里有个行业术语提醒，格雷格提到了“微型摄像机”（lipstick cameras）。

636
00:32:49.130 --> 00:32:57.170
Those are itty-bitty tiny cameras that they would put up in our visors in the car at an angle.
那是一种极小的摄像机，他们会以一定角度安装在车内的遮阳板上。

637
00:32:57.250 --> 00:33:01.350
And one would shoot one passenger and one would shoot the other passenger.
一个拍一个乘客，另一个拍另一个乘客。

638
00:33:02.350 --> 00:33:05.110
And we would just literally do what Greg said.
我们真的就按格雷格说的做。

639
00:33:05.290 --> 00:33:09.270
We would just drive around and we would have a little walkie-talkie in the car.
我们就在车里到处开，车里放着一个对讲机。

640
00:33:09.350 --> 00:33:15.430
And there would be a car either in front of us or behind us that had the crew, the director, a sound person.
在我们前面或后面会有一辆车，里面坐着摄制组、导演和录音师。

641
00:33:15.930 --> 00:33:17.110
They could hear us.
他们能听到我们说话。

642
00:33:17.210 --> 00:33:21.110
They could see us on a little like mobile video screen.
他们能通过一个小型的移动视频屏幕看到我们。

643
00:33:21.770 --> 00:33:24.030
And they would talk to us over the walkie-talkie.
他们会通过对讲机跟我们交流。

644
00:33:24.170 --> 00:33:25.610
And they would say, oh, that was great.
他们会说，哦，刚才那段很棒。

645
00:33:25.630 --> 00:33:26.510
We're going to do that again.
我们要再来一次。

646
00:33:27.110 --> 00:33:29.330
And then we would just drive around.
然后我们就继续开车。

647
00:33:29.530 --> 00:33:30.630
They would have police cars.
他们还会安排警车。

648
00:33:32.370 --> 00:33:37.390
Yeah, we had like the motorcycle police guys, too, who would sort of be in the front.
没错，我们还有那种摩托车警察，他们会在前面开道。

649
00:33:37.670 --> 00:33:45.810
And we'd have this path that was cleared for us so that, you know, we wouldn't have to drive around people who didn't know we were filming, right?
我们有一条清空的路线，这样我们就不用在不知情的路人中间穿梭了，对吧？

650
00:33:45.970 --> 00:33:46.770
So it was safe.
所以这样很安全。

651
00:33:47.550 --> 00:33:50.930
And we would just basically make a loop usually in one neighborhood.
我们基本上就是在同一个街区绕圈。

652
00:33:50.950 --> 00:33:53.210
We'd just make the same loop over and over.
我们只是反反复复地绕着同一个圈。

653
00:33:53.730 --> 00:33:56.870
Yeah, that was a whole thing that Kent Zabornak, a.k.a.
没错，那全靠肯特·扎博纳克（Kent Zabornak），也就是人称

654
00:33:57.030 --> 00:33:58.970
Kentopedia, he would have to clear that.
“肯特百科”的那位，他得去搞定审批。

655
00:33:58.970 --> 00:34:02.090
You'd have to call the highway patrol or the police.
你得给公路巡警或当地警察打电话。

656
00:34:02.090 --> 00:34:08.330
And they would give us a zone that we were allowed to use for a certain period of time on that day.
他们会划定一个区域，允许我们在当天的一定时间内使用。

657
00:34:09.150 --> 00:34:11.230
And we would just loop around.
然后我们就绕着圈开。

658
00:34:11.570 --> 00:34:16.250
And it was always difficult in Los Angeles to find a loop that didn't have any palm trees.
在洛杉矶想找一个没有棕榈树的环形路线总是很难。

659
00:34:16.250 --> 00:34:26.630
So we tend to film in the same neighborhoods over and over because clearly they found trees that looked possibly East Coast-ish, you know?
所以我们倾向于反复在同一个街区拍摄，因为显然那些地方的树看起来有点像东海岸的风格，你懂吧？

660
00:34:27.230 --> 00:34:27.430
Yes.
没错。

661
00:34:27.430 --> 00:34:29.850
We got to know these loops very well.
我们对这些路线非常熟悉。

662
00:34:30.210 --> 00:34:37.670
One of the things Dave Rogers said in the DVD commentary is that this was the first time that we used the lipstick cameras in the cars.
戴夫·罗杰斯（Dave Rogers）在DVD评论音轨里提到过一件事，这是我们第一次在车里使用微型摄像头。

663
00:34:37.670 --> 00:34:45.170
Previously, when we had done driving scenes, one of our camera operators, Randall or Matt, would be scrunched in the back seat with a camera.
以前拍开车戏时，我们的摄影师兰德尔（Randall）或马特（Matt）得蜷缩在后座扛着摄像机。

664
00:34:45.410 --> 00:34:51.270
And, you know, I noticed the video quality was a little different on the lipstick cameras when I was watching it.
而且，我注意到看的时候，微型摄像头的画质确实有点不一样。

665
00:34:51.410 --> 00:34:55.950
It's not quite as crisp as a Matt camera or a Randall camera.
不如马特或兰德尔拍出来的那么清晰。

666
00:34:56.570 --> 00:34:58.310
Look at you, Ms. Techie.
瞧瞧你，科技达人女士。

667
00:34:58.490 --> 00:34:59.830
You got a tech alert there?
你这是发现了什么技术细节吗？

668
00:34:59.990 --> 00:35:00.530
Look at you.
看你这样子。

669
00:35:00.730 --> 00:35:01.150
I noticed it.
我确实注意到了。

670
00:35:01.290 --> 00:35:02.110
I did.
我确实注意到了。

671
00:35:02.250 --> 00:35:06.430
So let's talk about all of these cars and all their driving around.
那我们来聊聊这些车和它们到处转悠的事吧。

672
00:35:06.970 --> 00:35:10.290
Well, the first scene we really see is Andy and Michael.
嗯，我们看到的第一个场景是安迪和迈克尔。

673
00:35:10.590 --> 00:35:16.470
And Andy is determined to use this one-on-one time with Michael to chip away at Dwight, right?
安迪决心利用这段和迈克尔独处的机会来离间德怀特，对吧？

674
00:35:16.710 --> 00:35:18.170
He's going to undermine him.
他打算拆他的台。

675
00:35:18.390 --> 00:35:19.710
He asks about the laundry.
他问起了洗衣房的事。

676
00:35:19.970 --> 00:35:24.510
Michael tells him that Dwight went to corporate to try to get his job.
迈克尔告诉他，德怀特曾去总部试图取代他的职位。

677
00:35:24.690 --> 00:35:28.170
And, oh, my gosh, Andy is, like, so happy to get this information.
天哪，安迪听到这个消息简直高兴坏了。

678
00:35:28.530 --> 00:35:28.890
Yes.
没错。

679
00:35:29.010 --> 00:35:33.910
He's going to spend this whole episode slowly chipping away at Dwight's reputation.
他这一整集都要花心思慢慢破坏德怀特的声誉。

680
00:35:34.270 --> 00:35:34.590
Yeah.
是啊。

681
00:35:34.590 --> 00:35:36.530
Well, then we see Phyllis.
接着我们看到了菲利斯。

682
00:35:36.710 --> 00:35:38.250
She pulls into a beauty salon.
她把车开进了一家美容院。

683
00:35:38.630 --> 00:35:42.670
Her and Karen are going to get some super glam makeovers.
她和凯伦要去化个超级华丽的妆。

684
00:35:42.890 --> 00:35:43.950
We don't know why.
我们不知道为什么。

685
00:35:44.190 --> 00:35:47.210
It looks like when you used to go to the mall to glamour shots.
看起来就像你以前去商场拍那种艺术照一样。

686
00:35:47.450 --> 00:35:48.210
Did you ever do that?
你拍过吗？

687
00:35:48.390 --> 00:35:52.230
I never did glamour shots, but my sister Emily did.
我没拍过艺术照，但我妹妹艾米丽拍过。

688
00:35:52.510 --> 00:35:55.930
Yes, I never did it either, but my sister Tina did.
是啊，我也没拍过，但我妹妹蒂娜拍过。

689
00:35:55.930 --> 00:36:01.670
And they gave her this enormous hairdo, like this bouffant hairdo, and all this makeup.
他们给她弄了个巨大的发型，那种蓬松的发髻，还化了浓妆。

690
00:36:01.750 --> 00:36:03.670
And I think, like, a feather boa.
我记得好像还有一条羽毛围巾。

691
00:36:05.210 --> 00:36:06.370
That was common.
那很常见。

692
00:36:06.370 --> 00:36:07.290
That was common.
确实很常见。

693
00:36:07.430 --> 00:36:11.350
And they would shoot you on a green screen and then sort of insert different backgrounds,
他们会让你站在绿幕前拍摄，然后后期合成各种背景，

694
00:36:11.390 --> 00:36:12.450
if I remember correctly.
如果我没记错的话。

695
00:36:12.810 --> 00:36:13.690
Like the Eiffel Tower.
比如埃菲尔铁塔之类的。

696
00:36:13.690 --> 00:36:14.910
Like they would.
没错，他们会那样做。

697
00:36:15.410 --> 00:36:15.930
Okay.
好吧。

698
00:36:16.190 --> 00:36:17.910
So that is what this makeover looks like.
所以这次大改造看起来就是那种风格。

699
00:36:18.070 --> 00:36:20.270
That might be like an old tech alert.
那可能算是一个过时的技术提醒吧。

700
00:36:20.450 --> 00:36:21.830
Does glamour shots still exist?
艺术照摄影店现在还存在吗？

701
00:36:22.250 --> 00:36:23.570
I don't think so, lady.
我不这么认为，女士。

702
00:36:23.810 --> 00:36:24.530
I don't think so.
我不这么认为。

703
00:36:24.650 --> 00:36:29.050
I think the era of the selfie and the iPhone, there aren't glamour.
我觉得在自拍和iPhone的时代，已经没有魅力可言了。

704
00:36:29.790 --> 00:36:30.630
And the filters.
还有滤镜。

705
00:36:30.810 --> 00:36:32.010
Glamour shots are no more.
魅力摄影已成往事。

706
00:36:32.910 --> 00:36:36.310
Well, then we also have Ryan and Stanley.
好吧，然后我们还有瑞安和斯坦利。

707
00:36:36.890 --> 00:36:41.070
And Ryan asked Stanley if he could take the lead on this sales call.
瑞安问斯坦利能不能让他主导这次销售电话。

708
00:36:41.230 --> 00:36:43.890
And Stanley is like, nothing would delight me more.
斯坦利说，没有什么比这更让我高兴的了。

709
00:36:44.370 --> 00:36:45.930
Oh, Stanley knows something.
哦，斯坦利肯定知道些什么。

710
00:36:45.930 --> 00:36:47.070
And he's tickled.
他乐坏了。

711
00:36:47.210 --> 00:36:47.930
He can't wait.
他迫不及待了。

712
00:36:48.230 --> 00:36:49.270
Oh, can't wait.
哦，迫不及待了。

713
00:36:49.410 --> 00:36:51.750
We will find out why in a little bit.
我们一会儿就会知道原因。

714
00:36:52.490 --> 00:36:58.930
So now, back at the office, while all this driving around is happening, Angela invites
现在回到办公室，当大家都在外面开车的时候，安吉拉邀请了

715
00:36:58.930 --> 00:37:00.290
Pam to coffee.
帕姆去喝咖啡。

716
00:37:00.290 --> 00:37:02.110
Yes, and Pam was like, what?
是的，帕姆当时心想，什么？

717
00:37:02.550 --> 00:37:03.350
But okay.
但还是答应了。

718
00:37:03.990 --> 00:37:08.490
Now, on a personal note, I was thrilled to do this scene.
现在，说点私人的，我当时非常激动能拍这场戏。

719
00:37:08.690 --> 00:37:13.650
You and I never got to do scenes together, let alone go on a location together.
你和我从来没一起拍过戏，更别提一起去外景地了。

720
00:37:13.810 --> 00:37:15.310
We were giddy, Jenna.
我们当时兴奋极了，珍娜。

721
00:37:15.550 --> 00:37:16.490
We couldn't wait.
我们等不及了。

722
00:37:16.670 --> 00:37:22.670
So some of that smiling and happiness you see in Angela Martin is just me being happy that
所以你在安吉拉·马丁身上看到的那些微笑和快乐，其实就是我因为

723
00:37:22.670 --> 00:37:24.410
I get to do a scene with my BFF.
能和我的闺蜜一起拍戏而感到高兴。

724
00:37:24.630 --> 00:37:25.950
And I get to be normal.
而且我还能表现得正常一点。

725
00:37:25.950 --> 00:37:28.530
I get to smile and not be snarky.
我可以微笑，不用尖酸刻薄。

726
00:37:29.130 --> 00:37:33.190
It was so—we were so excited, Angela, when we got this script.
安吉拉，当我们拿到这个剧本时，我们真的太兴奋了。

727
00:37:33.370 --> 00:37:33.630
Yeah.
是啊。

728
00:37:33.950 --> 00:37:36.010
All of my scenes are basically with you.
我所有的戏基本上都是和你一起拍的。

729
00:37:36.310 --> 00:37:38.210
Yeah, we had the same work day.
是啊，我们的工作时间是一样的。

730
00:37:38.210 --> 00:37:39.750
And then we had a few days off.
然后我们还有几天假。

731
00:37:39.790 --> 00:37:41.250
It was like—we were like, woo-hoo!
当时我们就像是，呜呼！

732
00:37:41.650 --> 00:37:43.630
It was kind of like BFF week.
那简直就像是闺蜜周。

733
00:37:43.850 --> 00:37:44.190
Yeah.
是啊。

734
00:37:44.290 --> 00:37:44.870
For us.
对我们来说。

735
00:37:46.190 --> 00:37:50.730
Well, some people pointed out that at the end of the scene, Pam grabs a notebook.
嗯，有些人指出在场景结束时，帕姆拿了一个笔记本。

736
00:37:51.910 --> 00:37:56.630
And people were wondering, why is Pam bringing a notebook to coffee?
大家都在纳闷，为什么帕姆去喝咖啡要带个笔记本？

737
00:37:56.790 --> 00:37:58.510
Is she going to take notes on Angela?
她是打算给安吉拉做记录吗？

738
00:37:59.290 --> 00:37:59.810
No.
不是。

739
00:38:00.410 --> 00:38:01.330
No, you guys.
不是的，伙计们。

740
00:38:01.490 --> 00:38:02.830
There was a line that got cut out.
有一句台词被剪掉了。

741
00:38:03.450 --> 00:38:05.470
Pam says to Angela, you know what?
帕姆对安吉拉说，你知道吗？

742
00:38:05.550 --> 00:38:07.430
I'll go around and take some coffee orders.
我去转转，顺便记下大家的咖啡订单。

743
00:38:07.750 --> 00:38:09.890
I'll see if anybody wants anything.
看看有没有人想要什么。

744
00:38:10.370 --> 00:38:10.810
Yes.
是的。

745
00:38:11.010 --> 00:38:12.270
This is in the deleted scenes.
这在删减片段里。

746
00:38:12.470 --> 00:38:13.150
She goes around.
她去转了一圈。

747
00:38:13.370 --> 00:38:15.110
Meredith gets really angry at you.
梅雷迪思对你非常生气。

748
00:38:15.270 --> 00:38:18.610
She's like, why would I pay $4 for milk and a cup?
她说，我为什么要花4美元买牛奶和杯子？

749
00:38:18.750 --> 00:38:20.170
And she's like, it's all angry.
她当时非常生气。

750
00:38:20.170 --> 00:38:22.150
Yeah, her and Creed get real cranky, right?
是啊，她和克里德都变得非常暴躁，对吧？

751
00:38:22.150 --> 00:38:24.930
Yeah, they get real cranky about the fancy coffee orders.
没错，他们对那些花哨的咖啡订单真的很挑剔。

752
00:38:25.550 --> 00:38:28.950
And there is a scene, Jenna, that just won't break your heart.
而且有一场戏，珍娜，那场戏简直让人心碎。

753
00:38:28.950 --> 00:38:34.610
Because when we come back with the coffee, it's clear that Toby only ordered coffee so
因为当我们带着咖啡回来时，很明显托比点咖啡只是为了

754
00:38:34.610 --> 00:38:36.350
he could have some interaction with Pam.
能和帕姆互动一下。

755
00:38:36.530 --> 00:38:41.210
But when she comes back with all the coffees and she's passing them around, she just hands
但当她带着所有咖啡回来分发时，她只是把咖啡

756
00:38:41.210 --> 00:38:43.270
it to Kelly, who then takes it to Toby.
递给了凯莉，凯莉随后又把它拿给了托比。

757
00:38:43.790 --> 00:38:47.390
And Toby just looks at Pam through the glass partition from the annex.
托比就隔着附楼的玻璃隔断看着帕姆。

758
00:38:47.590 --> 00:38:50.390
And he just puts the coffee in the trash.
然后他直接把咖啡扔进了垃圾桶。

759
00:38:50.530 --> 00:38:52.070
He didn't even get to talk to her.
他甚至都没能跟她说上话。

760
00:38:52.330 --> 00:38:53.070
Aw, Toby.
噢，托比。

761
00:38:53.470 --> 00:38:54.390
Poor Toby.
可怜的托比。

762
00:38:54.730 --> 00:38:55.210
Toby.
托比。

763
00:38:55.410 --> 00:38:56.070
So sad.
太难过了。

764
00:38:56.070 --> 00:39:03.330
Well, Ange, in the script, there is a scene where Pam is taking Toby's coffee order.
嗯，安吉，在剧本里，有一场戏是帕姆在记托比的咖啡订单。

765
00:39:03.610 --> 00:39:04.430
Oh, yeah?
噢，是吗？

766
00:39:04.630 --> 00:39:05.910
That's not in the deleted scenes.
那场戏不在删减片段里。

767
00:39:06.670 --> 00:39:07.310
Yeah.
是的。

768
00:39:07.310 --> 00:39:09.090
And he orders a chai latte.
他点了一杯印度拉茶拿铁。

769
00:39:09.190 --> 00:39:12.950
And Pam says, oh, my gosh, that's my coffee order.
帕姆说，天哪，那也是我点的咖啡。

770
00:39:13.150 --> 00:39:15.390
And he's like, oh, really?
他说，噢，真的吗？

771
00:39:15.550 --> 00:39:18.150
Oh, we have the same coffee order.
噢，我们点的咖啡一样。

772
00:39:19.230 --> 00:39:19.870
Yeah.
没错。

773
00:39:20.390 --> 00:39:20.870
Aw.
噢。

774
00:39:20.890 --> 00:39:25.350
So not only does he not get his coffee delivered by Pam,
所以他不仅没能让帕姆把咖啡送到他手里，

775
00:39:25.350 --> 00:39:28.730
he ordered a coffee he didn't even really drink,
他还点了一杯他其实根本没喝的咖啡，

776
00:39:28.730 --> 00:39:30.810
just to have something in common with her.
仅仅是为了和她有共同点。

777
00:39:31.810 --> 00:39:32.290
Toby.
托比。

778
00:39:32.650 --> 00:39:33.590
Wong, Wong.
哎，哎。

779
00:39:33.950 --> 00:39:36.030
He's stalking Pam and in love with her.
他在跟踪帕姆，而且爱上了她。

780
00:39:36.350 --> 00:39:39.170
So now, you guys, we're in the parking lot,
好了，各位，现在我们在停车场，

781
00:39:39.170 --> 00:39:41.030
and Dwight wants to amp himself up.
德怀特想让自己兴奋起来。

782
00:39:41.130 --> 00:39:43.590
He's got to get pumped for this sales call.
他得为这次销售拜访做好准备。

783
00:39:43.930 --> 00:39:46.550
Jim knows they have been on countless sales calls.
吉姆知道他们已经进行过无数次销售拜访了。

784
00:39:46.670 --> 00:39:47.830
He's like, you still do the thing?
他说，你还在做那个动作？

785
00:39:47.930 --> 00:39:49.190
And Dwight's like, just give me the keys.
德怀特说，把钥匙给我。

786
00:39:49.190 --> 00:39:50.630
And then he plays, like, I don't know,
然后他放了，我不知道，

787
00:39:50.710 --> 00:39:52.090
what is it, like, Motley Crue or something?
是什么，莫特利克鲁乐队的歌还是什么的？

788
00:39:52.290 --> 00:39:55.730
And once again, we see Dwight, like, rocking out,
再一次，我们看到德怀特像是在疯狂摇摆，

789
00:39:55.830 --> 00:39:57.190
doing air guitar to heavy metal,
对着重金属音乐弹空气吉他，

790
00:39:57.630 --> 00:40:00.710
like, punching the seat to get ready.
像是在捶打座椅来让自己进入状态。

791
00:40:01.410 --> 00:40:01.850
Yes.
是的。

792
00:40:02.330 --> 00:40:02.710
Yeah.
没错。

793
00:40:02.890 --> 00:40:05.210
This is his routine, I guess.
我想这就是他的例行公事。

794
00:40:05.430 --> 00:40:05.750
Yeah.
没错。

795
00:40:05.810 --> 00:40:06.590
And Jim knows it.
而且吉姆很清楚这一点。

796
00:40:06.730 --> 00:40:07.730
They're like old roommates.
他们就像老室友一样。

797
00:40:07.730 --> 00:40:08.650
He's like, here we go.
他心想，开始了。

798
00:40:08.950 --> 00:40:09.930
I stand out here.
我就站在外面。

799
00:40:10.110 --> 00:40:11.050
He does air guitar.
他弹着空气吉他。

800
00:40:12.890 --> 00:40:14.570
So he is amped up,
所以他兴奋起来了，

801
00:40:14.710 --> 00:40:16.510
because then when they're walking into the building,
因为当他们走进大楼时，

802
00:40:17.470 --> 00:40:18.870
Dwight has to be Dwight,
德怀特必须得是德怀特，

803
00:40:18.970 --> 00:40:20.450
and he's like, you go in first,
他会说，你先走，

804
00:40:21.570 --> 00:40:23.930
because he doesn't want to get attacked from behind.
因为他不想被从背后偷袭。

805
00:40:24.230 --> 00:40:26.750
Seven out of ten attacks are from the rear.
十次袭击里有七次是来自背后。

806
00:40:27.710 --> 00:40:28.150
Right.
没错。

807
00:40:28.270 --> 00:40:31.310
And Jim is like, well, what about the other 30%?
吉姆就说，那剩下的30%呢？

808
00:40:32.030 --> 00:40:33.670
And Dwight's like, I'd block it.
德怀特就说，我会挡住。

809
00:40:33.810 --> 00:40:34.710
I'd block it.
我会挡住。

810
00:40:34.790 --> 00:40:35.710
You can't get me.
你伤不到我。

811
00:40:36.670 --> 00:40:39.430
And then in, like, mid-sentence,
然后就在话说到一半的时候，

812
00:40:39.770 --> 00:40:42.850
Jim just hauls off and smacks Dwight,
吉姆突然出手给了德怀特一巴掌，

813
00:40:42.870 --> 00:40:44.330
and he is shocked.
他当时惊呆了。

814
00:40:44.330 --> 00:40:46.490
He can't believe he's been attacked from the front.
他不敢相信自己竟然会被从正面袭击。

815
00:40:46.990 --> 00:40:48.290
He can't believe it.
他简直不敢相信。

816
00:40:48.410 --> 00:40:49.890
Also, he's about to break.
而且，他快要憋不住笑了。

817
00:40:50.070 --> 00:40:51.130
Rain is about to laugh.
雷恩快要笑场了。

818
00:40:51.250 --> 00:40:52.750
You can totally see it.
你完全看得出来。

819
00:40:53.050 --> 00:40:54.870
At eight minutes, 50 seconds,
在八分五十秒的时候，

820
00:40:55.110 --> 00:40:56.090
Rain is about to laugh.
雷恩快要笑场了。

821
00:40:56.350 --> 00:40:57.670
Oh, 100%.
噢，百分之百。

822
00:40:57.670 --> 00:40:58.510
100%.
百分之百。

823
00:40:58.510 --> 00:41:00.630
Well, we had a fan question from Rachel Fortune.
我们收到一个来自瑞秋·福琼的粉丝提问。

824
00:41:00.970 --> 00:41:03.370
Was Jim supposed to slap Dwight
吉姆在他们走进大楼时

825
00:41:03.370 --> 00:41:04.430
as they walk in the building?
打德怀特那一巴掌是剧本安排的吗？

826
00:41:04.430 --> 00:41:06.890
Because Rain looked truly shocked.
因为雷恩看起来真的很震惊。

827
00:41:07.430 --> 00:41:11.170
Well, guys, this was a scripted moment.
伙计们，这确实是剧本里的桥段。

828
00:41:13.370 --> 00:41:16.570
But there's a reason why Rain was surprised,
但雷恩之所以会感到惊讶是有原因的，

829
00:41:16.570 --> 00:41:18.710
even though it was scripted.
尽管那是剧本写好的。

830
00:41:18.730 --> 00:41:20.690
And we asked Greg about it.
我们问过格雷格这件事。

831
00:41:20.930 --> 00:41:22.050
Here's what he had to say.
听听他是怎么说的。

832
00:41:22.430 --> 00:41:27.150
So some people asked about the Jim slapping Dwight moment.
有些人问到了吉姆打德怀特那一幕。

833
00:41:27.150 --> 00:41:30.970
So, you know, it's fun to think of the two of them
你知道，把他们俩想象成

834
00:41:31.870 --> 00:41:34.730
as being teamed up earlier in their career.
职业生涯早期的搭档是很有趣的。

835
00:41:34.910 --> 00:41:40.210
And we gave it kind of an Abbott and Costello comedy team feel,
我们给了它一种类似阿博特与科斯特洛那种喜剧搭档的感觉，

836
00:41:41.490 --> 00:41:43.510
you know, where Jim is, like, stopping short,
你知道，就是吉姆突然停下，

837
00:41:43.530 --> 00:41:44.710
so Dwight hits his head.
好让德怀特撞到头。

838
00:41:45.130 --> 00:41:49.590
And usually these little moments involve some comeuppance for Dwight.
通常这些小桥段都包含着对德怀特的一点小惩罚。

839
00:41:49.590 --> 00:41:53.650
And I remember John came up to me right before we were going to shoot
我记得在拍摄前，约翰走到我面前，

840
00:41:53.650 --> 00:41:56.490
the part where he hits Dwight in the face.
就在他要打德怀特脸的那场戏之前。

841
00:41:56.990 --> 00:42:00.170
And he said that he wanted to hit Rain for real a little bit harder
他说他想稍微用力一点真打雷恩，

842
00:42:00.170 --> 00:42:03.350
than they had worked out just to get a good startle out of him.
比他们之前排练的力度大一点，好让他表现出真实的惊吓。

843
00:42:03.470 --> 00:42:06.410
And I can't recall whether Rain was in on this,
我记不清雷恩是否知情了，

844
00:42:06.530 --> 00:42:08.430
but just didn't want to know which take.
或者只是不知道具体是哪一条。

845
00:42:08.890 --> 00:42:11.650
But we kind of worked out which take he was going to do.
但我们确实商量好了他要在哪一条动手。

846
00:42:11.650 --> 00:42:17.690
And I'm pretty sure we used the one where Rain was really startled
我很确定我们用了雷恩被约翰打得真正吓到的那一条。

847
00:42:17.690 --> 00:42:18.630
that John had hit him.
所以情况就是这样。

848
00:42:20.190 --> 00:42:21.610
So here's the deal.
在DVD评论音轨里，雷恩和约翰深入讨论过这个瞬间。

849
00:42:21.890 --> 00:42:25.830
On the DVD commentary, Rain and John talk in depth about this moment.
而且是雷恩要求约翰打他重一点的。

850
00:42:26.050 --> 00:42:29.210
And Rain asked John to hit him harder.
而且是雷恩要求约翰打他重一点的。

851
00:42:29.490 --> 00:42:32.110
He was like, I want you to hit me hard.
他当时说，我想让你狠狠地打我。

852
00:42:32.370 --> 00:42:33.950
And here's the thing about Rain.
关于雷恩，有一点要说。

853
00:42:34.090 --> 00:42:35.290
He's very method, you guys.
他非常讲究体验派，伙计们。

854
00:42:35.470 --> 00:42:38.250
When I slapped him, remember in Casino Night?
记得在“赌场之夜”那集，我扇他耳光的时候吗？

855
00:42:38.370 --> 00:42:38.610
Yeah.
记得。

856
00:42:38.870 --> 00:42:41.190
He said to me, Ange, you got to slap me harder.
他对我说，安吉，你得再用力点。

857
00:42:41.650 --> 00:42:42.110
Really?
真的吗？

858
00:42:42.370 --> 00:42:42.830
Slap me.
扇我。

859
00:42:43.090 --> 00:42:46.270
So in the DVD commentary, John was like, remember Rain?
所以在DVD评论音轨里，约翰说，还记得雷恩吗？

860
00:42:46.390 --> 00:42:47.430
You were like, slap me harder.
你当时说，再用力扇我。

861
00:42:47.510 --> 00:42:48.230
And I was like, OK.
我就说，好吧。

862
00:42:48.690 --> 00:42:51.230
And of course, that's the take they used
当然，他们用了那一版镜头，

863
00:42:51.230 --> 00:42:53.410
because Rain was legitimately like, oh,
因为雷恩当时确实是，噢，

864
00:42:53.970 --> 00:42:55.670
and then he almost started laughing.
然后他差点笑场了。

865
00:42:56.510 --> 00:42:59.710
Well, you can totally tell that he was taken aback.
嗯，完全看得出来他被吓了一跳。

866
00:42:59.970 --> 00:43:00.290
Yeah.
没错。

867
00:43:00.670 --> 00:43:04.730
And it ends up making a scripted moment look unscripted.
结果让一个剧本里的情节看起来像是即兴发挥的。

868
00:43:05.290 --> 00:43:06.990
But it was definitely scripted.
但那绝对是剧本写好的。

869
00:43:07.090 --> 00:43:08.490
I remember it said something like,
我记得剧本上写的是，

870
00:43:08.630 --> 00:43:11.310
Dwight gets smacked in the head by Jim.
德怀特被吉姆扇了一巴掌。

871
00:43:11.650 --> 00:43:14.510
And, you know, we would always have stunt coordinators come in
而且，你知道，我们每次需要触碰其他演员时，

872
00:43:14.510 --> 00:43:17.170
anytime we had to put our hands on another actor,
都会有特技指导到场，

873
00:43:17.370 --> 00:43:20.950
even if it was something that might be considered small, like a slap.
即使是像扇耳光这样看似微不足道的动作。

874
00:43:21.130 --> 00:43:23.950
And they actually teach you how to hit someone
他们会教你如何用手掌，

875
00:43:23.950 --> 00:43:27.810
with your palm in this certain sort of cupped way.
以某种特定的杯状方式去打人。

876
00:43:27.810 --> 00:43:32.370
So it makes a louder noise or it looks more violent than it really is.
这样声音会更响，看起来也比实际更暴力。

877
00:43:32.530 --> 00:43:37.150
And so, you know, we always had that training in us as well.
所以，你知道，我们一直都有接受那种训练。

878
00:43:37.350 --> 00:43:41.750
So I guess I should say Rain was not hurt in the execution of this,
所以我得说，雷恩在拍摄过程中并没有受伤，

879
00:43:41.870 --> 00:43:43.310
but he was certainly shocked.
但他确实被惊到了。

880
00:43:43.990 --> 00:43:44.890
Well, it worked.
嗯，效果很好。

881
00:43:44.890 --> 00:43:47.470
And it cracked Rain up and everyone else.
而且这让雷恩和其他人都笑喷了。

882
00:43:47.570 --> 00:43:48.790
And that's the take they picked.
最后他们选用了那一版镜头。

883
00:43:49.430 --> 00:43:51.290
So, lady, where are we?
那么，女士，我们现在到哪儿了？

884
00:43:51.430 --> 00:43:53.090
Are we going into some sales calls?
我们要开始讲那些销售电话了吗？

885
00:43:53.590 --> 00:43:54.410
We are.
是的。

886
00:43:54.650 --> 00:43:56.570
We're about to go into all these sales meetings,
我们马上要进入所有这些销售会议的内容了，

887
00:43:56.730 --> 00:43:57.650
but why don't we take a break?
但我们先休息一下好吗？

888
00:43:57.870 --> 00:43:59.790
And then we'll pick up right there in just a moment.
稍后我们再接着讲。

889
00:44:00.250 --> 00:44:00.590
Yeah.
好。

890
00:44:00.830 --> 00:44:10.560
All right.
好的。

891
00:44:10.560 --> 00:44:11.840
We are back.
我们回来了。

892
00:44:12.840 --> 00:44:15.140
Let's talk about all of these sales meetings.
来聊聊所有这些销售会议吧。

893
00:44:15.920 --> 00:44:16.360
Yes.
好的。

894
00:44:16.460 --> 00:44:18.760
I think the first one is Michael and Andy.
我想第一个是迈克尔和安迪的。

895
00:44:19.160 --> 00:44:22.680
And Jenna, once again, we see that Michael is a good salesman.
珍娜，我们再次看到迈克尔是个优秀的销售员。

896
00:44:22.680 --> 00:44:24.500
He knows how to connect with people.
他很懂得如何与人建立联系。

897
00:44:24.760 --> 00:44:26.120
He really does.
他确实很懂。

898
00:44:26.420 --> 00:44:27.200
He really does.
他真的很有本事。

899
00:44:27.360 --> 00:44:29.680
He doesn't know how to be someone's boss.
但他不知道该如何当好一个上司。

900
00:44:30.640 --> 00:44:31.960
That is his failing.
那是他的短板。

901
00:44:32.240 --> 00:44:35.700
He thinks that he's supposed to entertain you as a boss.
他觉得作为老板，他理应负责逗大家开心。

902
00:44:35.860 --> 00:44:36.040
Yeah.
是啊。

903
00:44:36.160 --> 00:44:38.880
But he does know how to connect with people one-on-one.
但他确实很擅长与人进行一对一的交流。

904
00:44:38.880 --> 00:44:41.760
And he really connects with this guy over fishing.
而且他和这个人因为钓鱼的话题聊得很投机。

905
00:44:42.140 --> 00:44:44.480
He compliments the fish that he caught.
他夸奖了对方钓到的鱼。

906
00:44:44.720 --> 00:44:47.220
And it's a callback to Lake Wall and Paw Pack.
这其实呼应了之前在瓦勒帕克湖的情节。

907
00:44:48.240 --> 00:44:49.380
Love a callback.
我很喜欢这种前后呼应。

908
