所以现在瑞安和斯坦利去教堂进行销售拜访。

1063
00:52:07.500 --> 00:52:13.780
And these four older, very sort of like dignified black men in their suits walk out to him.
然后有四位上了年纪、看起来非常庄重的黑人男士穿着西装向他们走来。

1064
00:52:14.040 --> 00:52:15.980
They're clearly an older generation.
他们显然是老一辈的人。

1065
00:52:16.220 --> 00:52:17.400
They're Stanley's generation.
他们是斯坦利那一代的。

1066
00:52:18.000 --> 00:52:23.780
And there's this young white kid who, Jenna, I don't think Ryan's been in a church in a while.
而瑞安这个年轻的白人小伙，珍娜，我觉得他很久没进过教堂了。

1067
00:52:24.960 --> 00:52:25.440
No.
没错。

1068
00:52:25.600 --> 00:52:32.760
And we've established that the way all these sales calls are successful is by people connecting with their client in some personal way.
我们已经确定了，所有这些销售拜访之所以能成功，是因为销售人员以某种个人方式与客户建立了联系。

1069
00:52:32.760 --> 00:52:36.460
And we quickly see that Ryan is going to have a hard time connecting with these gentlemen.
我们很快就能看出，瑞安很难与这些绅士建立联系。

1070
00:52:36.700 --> 00:52:38.200
And he just sort of starts stammering.
他开始结结巴巴的。

1071
00:52:38.400 --> 00:52:41.100
And he just keeps introducing himself over and over again.
他不停地重复做自我介绍。

1072
00:52:41.240 --> 00:52:41.560
Hi.
你好。

1073
00:52:41.900 --> 00:52:42.380
Hi.
你好。

1074
00:52:42.700 --> 00:52:43.180
Hi.
你好。

1075
00:52:43.180 --> 00:52:43.660
Hi.
你好。

1076
00:52:43.900 --> 00:52:44.220
Hi.
你好。

1077
00:52:44.220 --> 00:52:44.400
Hi.
你好。

1078
00:52:44.400 --> 00:52:47.140
And I love that Stanley's like, I'm not helping you.
我喜欢斯坦利那种“我才不帮你”的态度。

1079
00:52:47.140 --> 00:52:48.560
In fact, I'm just going to ignore you.
事实上，我打算直接无视你。

1080
00:52:48.700 --> 00:52:56.200
I'm going to turn away and do my crossword and let you just, what's the expression to know where it just, you flap in the wind.
我要转过身去填我的填字游戏，让你自己，那个表达怎么说来着，让你自己在风中凌乱。

1081
00:52:56.200 --> 00:52:56.860
Blow in the wind.
在风中飘摇。

1082
00:52:57.520 --> 00:52:57.840
Yeah.
对。

1083
00:52:57.980 --> 00:52:58.760
Something like that.
差不多就是那样。

1084
00:52:58.900 --> 00:53:00.980
He's just going to hang him out to dry there.
他就是要把他晾在那里不管。

1085
00:53:01.080 --> 00:53:01.740
It's so good.
太棒了。

1086
00:53:02.040 --> 00:53:05.980
I was able to find out the names of two of the clients, but I couldn't find names for the other guys.
我查到了其中两位客户的名字，但没能查到其他几位。

1087
00:53:05.980 --> 00:53:07.160
But Landon H.
不过兰登·H。

1088
00:53:07.260 --> 00:53:07.800
Lewis Jr.
小刘易斯。

1089
00:53:08.140 --> 00:53:09.480
And Leon Simmons Jr.
还有小莱昂·西蒙斯。

1090
00:53:09.540 --> 00:53:12.660
Are two of the clients in that scene.
是那一幕中的两位客户。

1091
00:53:12.900 --> 00:53:18.060
I also loved how all of the men in the scene were so much taller than BJ.
我也很喜欢那一幕里所有的男士都比BJ高出那么多。

1092
00:53:18.760 --> 00:53:19.320
Yes.
是的。

1093
00:53:19.460 --> 00:53:23.980
Because it really also made him just look so young, you know?
因为这确实让他看起来非常年轻，你懂吗？

1094
00:53:24.260 --> 00:53:24.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1095
00:53:24.820 --> 00:53:25.700
Next to them.
站在他们旁边。

1096
00:53:26.020 --> 00:53:27.180
Just the size difference.
就是体型上的差异。

1097
00:53:27.880 --> 00:53:28.500
Yes.
没错。

1098
00:53:28.500 --> 00:53:33.960
And then later when they're in the car, Angela, Stanley cannot stop laughing.
后来他们在车里的时候，安吉拉，斯坦利笑得停不下来。

1099
00:53:34.220 --> 00:53:38.340
There are all these shots that go back to them driving back to Dunder Mifflin.
有很多镜头切回他们开车回邓德·米夫林的路上。

1100
00:53:38.760 --> 00:53:42.300
And Stanley is just like, can't believe.
斯坦利简直就是，不敢相信。

1101
00:53:42.300 --> 00:53:44.300
He's so delighted by how that went.
他对自己刚才的表现感到非常满意。

1102
00:53:44.560 --> 00:53:45.500
He's so tickled.
他乐坏了。

1103
00:53:45.640 --> 00:53:46.980
It clearly made his day.
这显然让他开心了一整天。

1104
00:53:47.200 --> 00:53:52.840
I don't know that Stanley gets much joy out of working at Dunder Mifflin, but this was a real highlight for him.
我不知道斯坦利在邓德·米夫林工作能获得多少乐趣，但这对他来说确实是个高光时刻。

1105
00:53:52.840 --> 00:53:56.560
And there's this moment that Leslie talks about in the DVD.
莱斯利在DVD里提到了这样一个瞬间。

1106
00:53:56.900 --> 00:54:02.780
He said in the script, it was just that Stanley is driving and laughing, and they just kind of let him go.
他说剧本里原本只是写斯坦利在开车时大笑，然后他们就让他自由发挥了。

1107
00:54:02.940 --> 00:54:08.300
And he improvised the whole thing about, hi, hi, you sounded like my six-month-old niece.
他即兴发挥了整段内容，比如“嗨，嗨，你听起来像我六个月大的侄女”。

1108
00:54:08.460 --> 00:54:10.560
And like all of that, Leslie was just riffing.
所有这些，都是莱斯利即兴创作的。

1109
00:54:11.140 --> 00:54:12.820
Oh, that was so good.
噢，那太棒了。

1110
00:54:13.120 --> 00:54:13.880
I know.
我知道。

1111
00:54:13.880 --> 00:54:23.160
And he said, in fact, whenever Stanley would go off on Ryan, as he has throughout the show, they would just let Leslie just go.
他说，事实上，每当斯坦利像剧中那样训斥瑞安时，他们都会让莱斯利自由发挥。

1112
00:54:23.180 --> 00:54:25.600
And I think there's some amazing moments.
我觉得这其中有一些非常精彩的瞬间。

1113
00:54:26.000 --> 00:54:27.120
Oh, yes.
噢，是的。

1114
00:54:27.340 --> 00:54:27.680
Yes.
没错。

1115
00:54:28.180 --> 00:54:33.080
Well, you know, and this is Ryan's second sales call now that has not gone well.
嗯，你知道，这是瑞安第二次销售拜访，结果都不太顺利。

1116
00:54:33.360 --> 00:54:36.120
Remember, he went on the initiation sales call with Dwight.
记得吗，他之前和德怀特一起去过那次入职销售拜访。

1117
00:54:36.260 --> 00:54:37.520
They did not make the sale.
他们没谈成那笔生意。

1118
00:54:37.660 --> 00:54:40.240
And now he's gone out on this call with Stanley.
现在他又和斯坦利一起去拜访了。

1119
00:54:40.360 --> 00:54:42.640
Now, I believe Stanley's going to save this sale.
现在，我相信斯坦利会挽救这笔生意。

1120
00:54:42.640 --> 00:54:44.360
Oh, Stanley for sure saved it.
噢，斯坦利肯定挽救了它。

1121
00:54:44.560 --> 00:54:49.700
Okay, so while all of these sales meetings are happening, Pam and Angela are at the coffee shop.
好的，就在这些销售会议进行的同时，帕姆和安吉拉在咖啡店。

1122
00:54:49.940 --> 00:55:01.500
Angela is in such a great mood, and she's telling Pam a story about how she had this friend who was in need, and this gallant man came to her rescue.
安吉拉心情非常好，她正在给帕姆讲一个故事，说她有个朋友遇到了困难，然后一位英勇的男士挺身而出救了她。

1123
00:55:01.920 --> 00:55:02.260
Yeah.
嗯。

1124
00:55:02.620 --> 00:55:09.660
She's like, he must really care for her a lot because he did this wonderful thing for my friend.
她说，他一定非常关心她，因为他为我的朋友做了这件美妙的事。

1125
00:55:10.120 --> 00:55:10.560
Yeah.
嗯。

1126
00:55:10.740 --> 00:55:11.980
She's talking in code.
她在用暗语说话。

1127
00:55:12.640 --> 00:55:13.920
She's speaking in code.
她在说暗语。

1128
00:55:14.120 --> 00:55:17.060
She's like, my friend, let's call her Noel.
她说，我的朋友，我们就叫她诺埃尔吧。

1129
00:55:17.620 --> 00:55:20.860
And this gallant gentleman, we'll call him Kurt.
而这位英勇的绅士，我们就叫他库尔特吧。

1130
00:55:21.660 --> 00:55:26.440
Well, we all know that Kurt is Dwight's middle name, right?
嗯，我们都知道库尔特是德怀特的中间名，对吧？

1131
00:55:26.780 --> 00:55:27.100
Yes.
是的。

1132
00:55:27.100 --> 00:55:29.760
And we got a lot of fan questions about this, Angela.
安吉拉，我们收到了很多粉丝关于这个问题的提问。

1133
00:55:30.320 --> 00:55:46.020
Kenzie B., Elizabeth R., Julia Lee, Nicole Fink, and Katie Krull all want to know, when Angela refers to her friend Noel, is that because Noel is Angela's middle name?
肯齐·B、伊丽莎白·R、朱莉娅·李、妮可·芬克和凯蒂·克鲁尔都想知道，当安吉拉提到她的朋友诺埃尔时，是因为诺埃尔是安吉拉的中间名吗？

1134
00:55:46.920 --> 00:55:50.800
It definitely sounds like a very Angela's middle name.
听起来确实非常像安吉拉的中间名。

1135
00:55:51.440 --> 00:55:54.320
Well, yes, it is Angela's middle name.
嗯，是的，那确实是安吉拉的中间名。

1136
00:55:54.520 --> 00:55:59.280
Angela thinks she's being really savvy, but Pam totally knows who she's talking about.
安吉拉以为自己很聪明，但帕姆完全知道她在说谁。

1137
00:55:59.700 --> 00:56:01.580
But, yes, that is her middle name.
不过，是的，那确实是她的中间名。

1138
00:56:01.720 --> 00:56:03.540
But, Jenna, I have a question for you.
但是，珍娜，我有个问题想问你。

1139
00:56:04.420 --> 00:56:04.820
Okay.
好的。

1140
00:56:04.920 --> 00:56:06.820
Is Noel in the script?
剧本里写的是诺埃尔吗？

1141
00:56:07.000 --> 00:56:10.000
Because I have a little story about that middle name, and I'm curious.
因为关于那个中间名我有个小故事，我很好奇。

1142
00:56:10.000 --> 00:56:13.380
I think what was in the script was Colette.
我想剧本里写的是科莱特。

1143
00:56:14.360 --> 00:56:15.000
Okay.
好的。

1144
00:56:15.100 --> 00:56:21.660
I looked this up, and in the script, Angela actually says this.
我查了一下，在剧本里，安吉拉实际上是这么说的。

1145
00:56:21.680 --> 00:56:28.140
She says, well, a friend of mine, let's just call her, oh, let's just call her me.
她说，嗯，我有个朋友，我们就叫她，噢，我们就叫她我吧。

1146
00:56:28.700 --> 00:56:29.260
What?
什么？

1147
00:56:29.540 --> 00:56:30.540
And then you giggle.
然后你就咯咯笑了。

1148
00:56:31.600 --> 00:56:41.280
Okay, so my memory of this is when we were shooting it that day, that the writers were pitching me different middle names, like different things to say.
好的，我对那天的拍摄记忆是，编剧们当时在向我提议不同的中间名，比如让我说不同的名字。

1149
00:56:41.460 --> 00:56:43.700
I know in one of them it was Colette.
我知道其中一个版本是科莱特。

1150
00:56:43.860 --> 00:56:45.580
I have such a memory of saying that.
我清楚地记得我说过那个名字。

1151
00:56:46.860 --> 00:56:48.880
And then we said Noel.
然后我们说了诺埃尔（Noel）。

1152
00:56:48.880 --> 00:56:54.740
And I like Noel the best because it sounds very sort of Angela Martin, doesn't it?
我最喜欢诺埃尔这个名字，因为它听起来很有安吉拉·马丁的感觉，不是吗？

1153
00:56:54.740 --> 00:57:04.560
It's her love of Christmas, her love of the story of Christmas, that Noel would be her middle name, and that's the one we went with.
正是因为她对圣诞节的热爱，对圣诞故事的热爱，诺埃尔才成了她的中间名，我们最终选定了这个。

1154
00:57:04.940 --> 00:57:15.000
And Dave Rogers talks about it in the DVD commentary, and he goes, I remember it being Colette, and he thought maybe I improvised Noel, but I didn't.
戴夫·罗杰斯在DVD评论音轨里也提到了，他说记得当时是科莱特（Colette），他以为可能是我即兴发挥改成了诺埃尔，但其实不是。

1155
00:57:15.120 --> 00:57:16.240
That was a writer's pitch.
那是编剧提议的。

1156
00:57:16.420 --> 00:57:18.160
I mean, I think I was part of the dialogue.
我的意思是，我觉得我参与了对话。

1157
00:57:18.160 --> 00:57:22.100
I think we were pitching names, but that all sort of happened in the moment.
我想我们当时在商量名字，但那都是即兴发生的。

1158
00:57:22.520 --> 00:57:23.380
I love it.
我喜欢这个名字。

1159
00:57:23.380 --> 00:57:24.580
It's perfect.
太完美了。

1160
00:57:25.020 --> 00:57:31.940
It is such an Angela Noel Martin, and I believe that will appear on your wedding invitation.
这名字简直就是安吉拉·诺埃尔·马丁，我相信它会出现在你的结婚请柬上。

1161
00:57:32.320 --> 00:57:33.080
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1162
00:57:33.300 --> 00:57:36.360
It's now part of my character's show Bible.
它现在已经成为我角色背景设定的一部分了。

1163
00:57:37.060 --> 00:57:40.720
We had another fan catch in this scene, Angela.
安吉拉，这一幕里还有另一个粉丝发现的细节。

1164
00:57:40.980 --> 00:57:45.480
Sarah Rouse wrote in to say, Pam is holding a piece of paper at the coffee shop.
莎拉·劳斯来信说，帕姆在咖啡店里拿着一张纸。

1165
00:57:45.480 --> 00:57:48.220
What is that supposed to be, and what does it say?
那是什么东西，上面写了什么？

1166
00:57:48.540 --> 00:57:52.420
Well, Sarah, that was the list of coffee orders.
嗯，莎拉，那是咖啡订单列表。

1167
00:57:53.380 --> 00:57:54.980
From those deleted scenes.
来自那些被删减的片段。

1168
00:57:55.480 --> 00:58:00.280
I had all the coffee orders written down on that piece of paper, and I was going to use it to make my order.
我把所有的咖啡订单都写在那张纸上了，我打算照着它去点单。

1169
00:58:00.560 --> 00:58:09.400
Well, Angela, also in this scene, just because we were talking about it earlier, your flower hairdo is on full display.
嗯，安吉拉，同样是在这一幕里，既然我们刚才提到了，你的花朵发型可是完全展示出来了。

1170
00:58:09.400 --> 00:58:17.000
Okay, just if you really want some great shots of it, guys, here it is, her WTF hairdo right here.
好吧，如果你们真的想看它的特写，伙计们，就在这儿，她那个“搞什么鬼”的发型。

1171
00:58:17.480 --> 00:58:17.840
WTF.
搞什么鬼。

1172
00:58:18.020 --> 00:58:18.760
Well, wait, wait.
等等，等等。

1173
00:58:18.840 --> 00:58:19.700
I have something to share.
我有东西要分享。

1174
00:58:19.700 --> 00:58:27.880
So, while we were on a break, I had been texting Kim Ferry about this hair, and she texted back, and so this is what she had to say about it.
刚才休息的时候，我一直在给金·费里发短信讨论这个发型，她回信了，这就是她对此的说法。

1175
00:58:28.080 --> 00:58:28.640
I said, Kim.
我说，金。

1176
00:58:28.640 --> 00:58:30.700
Oh, my gosh, it's a real-time tidbit.
天哪，这是实时的花絮。

1177
00:58:30.860 --> 00:58:32.040
It's a real-time tidbit.
这是实时的花絮。

1178
00:58:32.040 --> 00:58:33.600
It just came in a few minutes ago.
几分钟前刚收到的。

1179
00:58:33.600 --> 00:58:39.240
So, I said, Kim, what was the inspiration for this bun?
所以我问，金，这个发髻的灵感是什么？

1180
00:58:39.520 --> 00:58:45.500
I mean, I know that we thought my character was going to, like, be in a great mood, and so we wanted to try something new.
我是说，我知道我们当时觉得我的角色心情应该很好，所以想尝试点新鲜的。

1181
00:58:45.500 --> 00:58:48.540
She said, yes, here is the inspiration.
她说，没错，灵感来源如下。

1182
00:58:48.540 --> 00:58:55.260
She said, my first job in the business was working on a sci-fi show called Babylon 5.
她说，我入行后的第一份工作是在一部叫《巴比伦5号》的科幻剧组。

1183
00:58:56.100 --> 00:59:05.100
I worked on this show for five years, and I couldn't use any contemporary hairstyles because they wanted the hairstyles to look futuristic.
我在那部剧工作了五年，我不能用任何现代发型，因为他们要求发型看起来有未来感。

1184
00:59:05.620 --> 00:59:17.160
So, I started coming up with all these different kind of braids and buns with wires and fancy updos and Zulu knots, basically anything different that I could think of.
所以我开始设计各种各样的编发和发髻，用上发丝、花哨的盘发和祖鲁结，基本上任何我能想到的不同设计。

1185
00:59:17.160 --> 00:59:25.000
And your bun with those fun swirls was a good one for me because I had done it on Babylon 5.
你那个带有有趣旋涡的发髻对我来说很顺手，因为我在《巴比伦5号》里做过。

1186
00:59:25.320 --> 00:59:30.400
It's fast and easy, but technically, this is a sci-fi hairstyle.
它又快又简单，但从技术上讲，这是一款科幻发型。

1187
00:59:30.880 --> 00:59:33.880
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1188
00:59:34.120 --> 00:59:35.320
Isn't that great?
这不是很棒吗？

1189
00:59:36.340 --> 00:59:40.180
Don't you feel like Dwight would have loved it because he was Mr. Sci-Fi?
你不觉得德怀特会很喜欢吗？因为他可是科幻迷先生。

1190
00:59:41.140 --> 00:59:41.780
Yes.
是的。

1191
00:59:42.400 --> 00:59:46.480
Yes, no wonder she did her hair in this Babylon 5 hairstyle.
没错，难怪她弄了这个《巴比伦5号》的发型。

1192
00:59:47.160 --> 00:59:50.380
To thank Dwight for his, like, favor.
为了感谢德怀特帮了她忙。

1193
00:59:50.880 --> 00:59:51.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1194
00:59:51.640 --> 00:59:55.400
So, yes, this hairstyle inspired by Babylon 5.
所以，没错，这个发型灵感来自《巴比伦5号》。

1195
00:59:55.540 --> 00:59:57.020
It's the sci-fi bun.
这就是科幻发髻。

1196
00:59:58.640 --> 01:00:00.380
I don't think I could love that more.
我想我再也不会比现在更喜欢它了。

1197
01:00:00.860 --> 01:00:02.960
Kim Ferry, thank you for the real-time tidbit.
金·费里，谢谢你提供的实时花絮。

1198
01:00:03.280 --> 01:00:04.280
Thank you, Kim Ferry.
谢谢你，金·费里。

1199
01:00:04.960 --> 01:00:07.940
Sam just wrote, beats, bears, Babylon 5.
萨姆刚发来消息说：甜菜、熊、巴比伦5号。

1200
01:00:09.260 --> 01:00:10.640
Beats, oh, wait, here we go.
甜菜，噢，等等，开始了。

1201
01:00:10.820 --> 01:00:13.460
Bears, beats, Babylon 5 buns.
熊、甜菜、《巴比伦5号》小圆面包。

1202
01:00:13.460 --> 01:00:19.100
Oh, okay, so now everybody is coming back from their sales calls.
哦，好吧，现在大家都从销售拜访回来了。

1203
01:00:19.380 --> 01:00:20.100
Everyone's done.
大家都忙完了。

1204
01:00:20.320 --> 01:00:25.520
And we have this amazing scene in the car with Karen and Phyllis.
我们有一场凯伦和菲利斯在车里的精彩戏份。

1205
01:00:26.300 --> 01:00:33.320
Phyllis is so good in this scene because, you guys, she is going to reveal such a big plot point,
菲利斯在这场戏里表现得太棒了，伙计们，她即将揭露一个重大的剧情点，

1206
01:00:33.320 --> 01:00:36.080
and she just throws it away, right?
而她就那么轻描淡写地说了出来，对吧？

1207
01:00:36.440 --> 01:00:39.060
It's not, like, belabored in any way.
一点也不拖泥带水。

1208
01:00:39.100 --> 01:00:41.020
It's so perfect.
太完美了。

1209
01:00:41.900 --> 01:00:42.460
Yeah.
没错。

1210
01:00:42.840 --> 01:00:46.360
She's like, Karen, I had a lot of fun with you today.
她说，凯伦，我今天和你在一起玩得很开心。

1211
01:00:46.480 --> 01:00:48.280
I really enjoy spending time with you.
我很享受和你在一起的时光。

1212
01:00:48.420 --> 01:00:49.300
They're bonding.
她们在建立感情。

1213
01:00:49.300 --> 01:00:50.460
They feel good.
她们感觉很好。

1214
01:00:50.460 --> 01:00:56.280
And then she just very offhandedly says, and I'm really glad you're with Jim.
然后她非常随口地说，我真高兴你和吉姆在一起。

1215
01:00:56.580 --> 01:01:02.360
It makes me really happy because, you know, he was really hung up on Pam for such a long time.
这让我很高兴，因为你知道，他曾对帕姆念念不忘那么久。

1216
01:01:02.620 --> 01:01:04.640
And she's not even looking at Karen.
而且她甚至都没看凯伦。

1217
01:01:04.800 --> 01:01:06.200
She's looking in a rearview mirror.
她在看后视镜。

1218
01:01:06.360 --> 01:01:06.920
She's turning.
她在转弯。

1219
01:01:07.120 --> 01:01:07.760
She's just driving.
她只是在开车。

1220
01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:10.080
She's sort of saying something off the cuff.
她就像是随口说了一句什么。

1221
01:01:10.240 --> 01:01:11.980
And it's that much more powerful.
这让它显得更有冲击力。

1222
01:01:11.980 --> 01:01:17.900
And then Rashida, oh, my gosh, her reaction is so perfect.
然后拉什达，天哪，她的反应太完美了。

1223
01:01:18.840 --> 01:01:20.700
It's a fantastic scene.
这是一场精彩的戏。

1224
01:01:20.900 --> 01:01:21.840
Fantastic scene.
精彩的戏。

1225
01:01:22.140 --> 01:01:25.600
I feel like her pulse stops for a second.
我觉得她的脉搏停了一秒。

1226
01:01:25.760 --> 01:01:29.400
Like, I feel like I can see the wind go out of her, right?
就像，我觉得我能看到她泄了气一样，对吧？

1227
01:01:29.980 --> 01:01:31.280
Yes, I do, too.
是的，我也是。

1228
01:01:32.360 --> 01:01:37.800
You just, you see it hit her like a freight train, but she can't react.
你就是能看到它像货运列车一样撞向她，但她却无法做出反应。

1229
01:01:38.320 --> 01:01:38.640
Yeah.
没错。

1230
01:01:38.900 --> 01:01:40.280
The way it's really hitting her.
那种真正冲击她的方式。

1231
01:01:40.480 --> 01:01:41.700
It's so well done.
做得太好了。

1232
01:01:41.700 --> 01:01:44.060
These ladies did such a great job.
这两位女士表现得太棒了。

1233
01:01:44.740 --> 01:01:45.720
I agree.
我同意。

1234
01:01:46.220 --> 01:01:46.820
Yes.
是的。

1235
01:01:47.660 --> 01:01:51.340
Well, Andy is the first person to actually get back to the office.
安迪是第一个回到办公室的人。

1236
01:01:51.980 --> 01:01:56.920
And he starts, he starts sneaking around Dwight's desk.
他开始在德怀特的办公桌周围鬼鬼祟祟地摸索。

1237
01:01:57.120 --> 01:01:58.580
He goes through his car.
他翻了他的车。

1238
01:01:58.980 --> 01:01:59.140
Yeah.
没错。

1239
01:01:59.280 --> 01:02:00.480
Andy is a total snake.
安迪真是个彻头彻尾的阴险小人。

1240
01:02:00.740 --> 01:02:02.020
I mean, what the heck?
我是说，搞什么鬼？

1241
01:02:02.200 --> 01:02:02.740
I know.
我知道。

1242
01:02:02.980 --> 01:02:09.200
And he finds this toll booth receipt that proves that Dwight was in New York this morning.
他发现了一张过路费收据，证明德怀特今天早上在纽约。

1243
01:02:09.200 --> 01:02:11.780
He didn't oversleep like he claimed.
他并没有像他声称的那样睡过头。

1244
01:02:11.840 --> 01:02:13.340
And he marches into Michael's office.
然后他大步走进迈克尔的办公室。

1245
01:02:13.340 --> 01:02:15.940
And he's like, I found this toll booth receipt.
他说，我发现了这张过路费收据。

1246
01:02:16.500 --> 01:02:18.100
I wonder what he was doing.
我想知道他在做什么。

1247
01:02:18.500 --> 01:02:20.540
Was he, maybe he was talking to Jan.
他是不是，也许他是在和简谈话。

1248
01:02:20.900 --> 01:02:23.420
And then he says, like, I seem to kind of remember.
然后他说，我好像记得。

1249
01:02:23.420 --> 01:02:28.660
I don't know who told me this, even though, Jenna, this was like, like an hour ago.
我不知道是谁告诉我的，尽管，珍娜，这明明就是一小时前的事。

1250
01:02:28.760 --> 01:02:30.420
He's like, I don't know who told me this.
他说，我不知道是谁告诉我的。

1251
01:02:30.540 --> 01:02:31.020
It was something.
那真是一段经历。

1252
01:02:31.260 --> 01:02:35.360
And then he has maybe one of my favorite quotes of this episode.
然后他说出了这一集里我最喜欢的台词之一。

1253
01:02:35.360 --> 01:02:36.640
He was like, there's a story.
他说，这背后有个故事。

1254
01:02:36.780 --> 01:02:37.140
I don't know.
我不知道。

1255
01:02:37.220 --> 01:02:39.460
It was about laundry and betrayal.
是关于洗衣服和背叛的故事。

1256
01:02:40.360 --> 01:02:45.020
In my mind, this is now a lifetime movie called Laundry and Betrayal.
在我脑海里，这已经是一部叫《洗衣服与背叛》的电视电影了。

1257
01:02:45.020 --> 01:02:46.180
I want to see it.
我想看这部电影。

1258
01:02:48.260 --> 01:02:48.760
Yes.
没错。

1259
01:02:49.360 --> 01:02:49.860
Yes.
是的。

1260
01:02:50.720 --> 01:02:51.860
Laundry and Betrayal.
《洗衣服与背叛》。

1261
01:02:51.980 --> 01:02:53.060
I want to see this film.
我想看这部电影。

1262
01:02:53.300 --> 01:02:53.880
I do, too.
我也是。

1263
01:02:54.560 --> 01:02:56.320
Well, so Michael calls Jan.
好吧，迈克尔给简打了电话。

1264
01:02:57.780 --> 01:03:00.760
And Jan is like, well, I didn't speak to Dwight.
简说，我没跟德怀特谈过。

1265
01:03:00.860 --> 01:03:04.240
But he did not give a reason for why he was here.
但他没说他为什么去那儿。

1266
01:03:04.720 --> 01:03:05.000
Yes.
是的。

1267
01:03:05.160 --> 01:03:06.920
This is my kid's favorite part.
这是我孩子最喜欢的部分。

1268
01:03:07.080 --> 01:03:11.880
My kid's favorite part is Jan goes, he did sign into the security sign-in sheet.
我孩子最喜欢的部分是简说，他在安保登记表上签了名。

1269
01:03:11.880 --> 01:03:17.480
But understate your business, he wrote, Beeswax, not yours, Incorporated.
但在写来访事由时，他写的是：不关你事有限公司。

1270
01:03:17.900 --> 01:03:19.520
I love that, too.
我也很喜欢那个。

1271
01:03:19.580 --> 01:03:21.100
My kids loved that.
我孩子们也喜欢那个。

1272
01:03:21.300 --> 01:03:25.000
Well, when Dwight gets back to the office, Michael confronts him.
好吧，当德怀特回到办公室时，迈克尔质问了他。

1273
01:03:26.060 --> 01:03:27.480
He's like, where were you?
他说，你去哪儿了？

1274
01:03:27.620 --> 01:03:28.400
Tell me where you were.
告诉我你去哪儿了。

1275
01:03:28.520 --> 01:03:29.820
And Dwight will not say.
但德怀特就是不说。

1276
01:03:29.940 --> 01:03:31.720
He won't say where he was.
他就是不肯说他去哪儿了。

1277
01:03:31.960 --> 01:03:32.980
He overslept.
他睡过头了。

1278
01:03:33.080 --> 01:03:34.240
The damn rooster didn't crow.
该死的公鸡没打鸣。

1279
01:03:34.980 --> 01:03:35.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1280
01:03:36.320 --> 01:03:40.000
But he will not, he will not fess up.
但他就是不肯，就是不肯坦白。

1281
01:03:40.620 --> 01:03:42.260
And this becomes a problem.
这成了一个问题。

1282
01:03:42.560 --> 01:03:43.960
And Pam knows why.
而帕姆知道原因。

1283
01:03:44.600 --> 01:03:46.720
Pam and Angela are exchanging looks.
帕姆和安吉拉在交换眼色。

1284
01:03:46.900 --> 01:03:48.140
Angela is sweating it.
安吉拉急得直冒汗。

1285
01:03:48.380 --> 01:03:50.920
She's horrified that Dwight's going through this.
她很害怕德怀特要经历这些。

1286
01:03:51.040 --> 01:03:53.560
But she doesn't want people to know about them.
但她不想让别人知道他们的关系。

1287
01:03:53.740 --> 01:03:55.980
It's very layered emotionally for Angela.
这对安吉拉来说情感层面非常复杂。

1288
01:03:56.540 --> 01:04:02.880
Well, it leads to a break room scene with Dwight and Angela, where you are, again, not facing one another.
嗯，这导致了休息室里德怀特和安吉拉的一场戏，你们俩又是背对着彼此。

1289
01:04:03.100 --> 01:04:06.480
One of your famous, famous break room scenes.
你们那些著名的休息室场景之一。

1290
01:04:06.480 --> 01:04:09.820
There's a little bit of heartbreak in the break room in this scene.
这一幕的休息室里带有一点心碎的感觉。

1291
01:04:10.200 --> 01:04:12.580
Oh, lady, I noticed it, too.
噢，女士，我也注意到了。

1292
01:04:13.140 --> 01:04:14.120
Here's what we had.
这是我们收到的作品。

1293
01:04:14.420 --> 01:04:17.480
My mama knitted me in a sexy sweater.
我妈妈为我织了一件性感毛衣。

1294
01:04:30.560 --> 01:04:32.280
That was by Michelle Ferguson.
那是米歇尔·弗格森的作品。

1295
01:04:32.580 --> 01:04:34.980
Michelle, you know how much we love that song.
米歇尔，你知道我们有多喜欢那首歌。

1296
01:04:35.140 --> 01:04:35.880
We love it.
我们很喜欢它。

1297
01:04:36.360 --> 01:04:36.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1298
01:04:37.000 --> 01:04:38.940
Michelle, I literally listen to it all the time.
米歇尔，我真的经常听这首歌。

1299
01:04:39.060 --> 01:04:40.240
It's super catchy.
它超级洗脑。

1300
01:04:40.580 --> 01:04:41.660
It's very catchy.
非常洗脑。

1301
01:04:41.880 --> 01:04:42.720
I really love it.
我真的很喜欢。

1302
01:04:42.800 --> 01:04:44.440
Someone give this woman a music contract.
快给这位女士一份音乐合约。

1303
01:04:44.860 --> 01:04:45.940
We'll buy it.
我们要买下它。

1304
01:04:46.080 --> 01:04:46.460
Okay.
好的。

1305
01:04:46.840 --> 01:04:47.840
We love it.
我们很喜欢。

1306
01:04:47.840 --> 01:04:54.780
Yeah, so Dwight is like, listen, why don't we just come clean and, you know, let people know our love for one another?
是啊，德怀特当时说，听着，我们为什么不坦白呢，你知道，让大家知道我们对彼此的爱？

1307
01:04:55.000 --> 01:04:56.940
So this scene actually went on.
所以这一幕其实还有后续。

1308
01:04:57.120 --> 01:05:05.860
It's not in the deleted scenes, but we did shoot a little bit longer of a version where, as I cry behind me, Dwight's like, don't cry, monkey.
虽然不在删减片段里，但我们确实拍了一个更长的版本，当我躲在后面哭的时候，德怀特说，别哭，小猴子。

1309
01:05:06.560 --> 01:05:07.800
Monkeys don't cry.
猴子是不会哭的。

1310
01:05:09.220 --> 01:05:11.600
Aw, I kind of wish that was still in there.
噢，我真希望那段还在里面。

1311
01:05:11.720 --> 01:05:12.320
I know.
我知道。

1312
01:05:13.440 --> 01:05:22.580
Well, Angela, a few people wrote in about this scene because they noted that when you start dating Andy, you have no problem with everyone in the office knowing it.
嗯，安吉拉，有些人写信问到这一幕，因为他们注意到当你开始和安迪约会时，你一点也不介意办公室里的每个人都知道。

1313
01:05:23.120 --> 01:05:26.920
Oh, well, Angela, revenge dates Andy, you guys.
噢，好吧，安吉拉，那是为了报复才和安迪约会的，各位。

1314
01:05:27.400 --> 01:05:33.260
Andy's not her true love that she wants to protect and keep all to herself because it's so special.
安迪不是她想要保护并独自占有的真爱，因为那份爱太特别了。

1315
01:05:33.260 --> 01:05:37.520
Well, she's starting to date Andy because she's mad as hell at Dwight.
嗯，她开始和安迪约会是因为她对德怀特气疯了。

1316
01:05:38.080 --> 01:05:38.720
Right.
没错。

1317
01:05:38.940 --> 01:05:40.100
Very different motivation.
动机完全不同。

1318
01:05:40.440 --> 01:05:40.880
Right.
没错。

1319
01:05:41.180 --> 01:05:45.120
In the meantime, Karen and Jim have gone to coffee.
与此同时，凯伦和吉姆去喝咖啡了。

1320
01:05:45.120 --> 01:05:50.040
And Karen is going to ask Jim if he had feelings for Pam.
凯伦打算问吉姆是否对帕姆有过感情。

1321
01:05:50.300 --> 01:05:52.520
And lady, I have a clip.
女士们，我有个片段。

1322
01:05:52.960 --> 01:05:58.380
Sam, play the clip because everything you need to know is right here, Karen.
山姆，播放片段，因为你需要知道的一切都在这里了，凯伦。

1323
01:05:58.700 --> 01:06:00.460
Why couldn't you hear it?
你为什么听不出来呢？

1324
01:06:01.180 --> 01:06:02.220
Let me ask you a question.
让我问你个问题。

1325
01:06:02.460 --> 01:06:02.680
Okay.
好的。

1326
01:06:03.720 --> 01:06:05.500
Did you ever have a thing for Pam?
你曾经对帕姆有意思吗？

1327
01:06:06.360 --> 01:06:07.000
Pam?
帕姆？

1328
01:06:07.480 --> 01:06:09.540
Did I ever have a thing for her?
我曾经对她有意思？

1329
01:06:10.060 --> 01:06:10.480
No.
没有。

1330
01:06:11.680 --> 01:06:12.320
Why?
为什么？

1331
01:06:12.540 --> 01:06:13.260
Did she say something?
她说了什么吗？

1332
01:06:15.260 --> 01:06:15.700
There!
看吧！

1333
01:06:15.700 --> 01:06:18.100
That's all you need to know, Karen.
这就是你需要知道的一切，凯伦。

1334
01:06:18.380 --> 01:06:20.260
He clearly has a thing for her.
他显然对她有意思。

1335
01:06:20.440 --> 01:06:22.560
But, oh, poor Karen.
但是，噢，可怜的凯伦。

1336
01:06:22.780 --> 01:06:25.860
She, you know, he convinces her that he doesn't.
她，你知道，他让她相信他没有。

1337
01:06:26.120 --> 01:06:28.120
Maybe he's not ready to admit it, right?
也许他还没准备好承认，对吧？

1338
01:06:28.280 --> 01:06:31.440
And she is not ready to really see truth.
而她也没准备好真正面对真相。

1339
01:06:31.540 --> 01:06:34.060
But you know down deep she knows.
但你知道，她内心深处是知道的。

1340
01:06:35.040 --> 01:06:38.180
Well, lady, she says, I moved here.
嗯，女士，她说，我搬到这里来了。

1341
01:06:38.400 --> 01:06:38.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1342
01:06:39.260 --> 01:06:40.600
I moved here.
我搬到这里来了。

1343
01:06:40.760 --> 01:06:44.380
And I think that's the part of Karen that doesn't want to see the truth
我觉得那是凯伦不想面对真相的那一部分，

1344
01:06:44.380 --> 01:06:52.140
because it's a little humiliating to deal with the fact that you moved somewhere for the wrong person.
因为不得不面对自己为了错误的人搬到某个地方的事实，是有点丢脸的。

1345
01:06:52.380 --> 01:06:52.560
Exactly.
没错。

1346
01:06:52.640 --> 01:06:56.940
We all have a friend who has moved somewhere for someone and then it didn't work out.
我们都有一个朋友，为了某人搬到某个地方，结果却没能在一起。

1347
01:06:57.160 --> 01:06:57.820
It's devastating.
那真是太令人崩溃了。

1348
01:06:58.520 --> 01:07:01.880
But then they hang on to it because they moved.
但他们还是坚持着，因为他们已经搬过去了。

1349
01:07:02.100 --> 01:07:02.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1350
01:07:02.560 --> 01:07:07.000
And it's like you want, you're willing it to be right even though you know it's wrong.
就像你想要，你强迫自己相信那是对的，尽管你知道那是错的。

1351
01:07:07.500 --> 01:07:13.020
So this is the moment where I know we've been coming down kind of hard on Wishy-Washy Jim.
所以，我知道我们对“优柔寡断的吉姆”有点太苛刻了，就是现在这一刻。

1352
01:07:13.020 --> 01:07:18.080
But this is the moment where Karen is now not reading the signals.
但现在这一刻，凯伦却没读懂这些信号。

1353
01:07:19.480 --> 01:07:20.180
No.
没错。

1354
01:07:20.580 --> 01:07:21.080
No.
没错。

1355
01:07:21.420 --> 01:07:27.320
So, Ange, should we go back to Dunder Mifflin to this grand announcement from Dwight?
